window.FERN_DATA = window.FERN_DATA || {};
FERN_DATA["java"] = {"units": [{"id": "foundations", "title": "Foundations", "blurb": "How a Java program is built, compiled and run, and how it stores data.", "topics": [{"id": "computer-basics", "title": "Computer basics", "src": "Ch. 1", "idea": "A computer is hardware (physical parts) run by software (instructions). The CPU runs instructions, memory holds them while the program runs, and storage keeps data permanently.", "deep": "<ul>\n<li><strong>Hardware:</strong> the physical parts: CPU, memory, motherboard, storage, monitor, keyboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Software:</strong> the programs and instructions that tell the hardware what to do.</li>\n<li><strong>Program:</strong> a set of instructions a computer follows. Programming means writing them.</li>\n<li><strong>CPU (central processing unit):</strong> the \"brain\". It fetches instructions from memory and executes them.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory (RAM):</strong> holds data and instructions while the computer runs. It is <em>volatile</em>: it loses everything when the power goes off.</li>\n<li><strong>Storage:</strong> hard drives, SSDs, USB drives. Data stays when the power is off.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bits and bytes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computers only use two values: 0 and 1.</li>\n<li>A <strong>bit</strong> is one binary digit. A <strong>byte</strong> is 8 bits.</li>\n<li>1 KB ≈ 1,000 bytes · 1 MB ≈ 1 million · 1 GB ≈ 1 billion · 1 TB ≈ 1,000 GB</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Levels of programming languages</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Machine language:</strong> binary instructions the CPU understands directly.</li>\n<li><strong>Assembly language:</strong> short words or symbols instead of pure binary. Still low level.</li>\n<li><strong>High-level languages</strong> (Java, Python, C++): closer to English, easier for humans. Code written in one is called <strong>source code</strong>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "hardware: the physical parts: cpu, memory, motherboard, storage, monitor, keyboard. software: the programs and instructions that tell the hardware what to do. program: a set of instructions a computer follows. programming means writing them. cpu (central processing unit): the \"brain\". it fetches instructions from memory and executes them. memory (ram): holds data and instructions while the computer runs. it is volatile : it loses everything when the power goes off. storage: hard drives, ssds, usb drives. data stays when the power is off. bits and bytes computers only use two values: 0 and 1. a bit is one binary digit. a byte is 8 bits. 1 kb ≈ 1,000 bytes · 1 mb ≈ 1 million · 1 gb ≈ 1 billion · 1 tb ≈ 1,000 gb levels of programming languages machine language: binary instructions the cpu understands directly. assembly language: short words or symbols instead of pure binary. still low level. high-level languages (java, python, c++): closer to english, easier for humans. code written in one is called source code ."}, {"id": "how-java-runs", "title": "How Java runs", "src": "Ch. 1", "idea": "You write source code in a .java file. The compiler (javac) turns it into bytecode, and the JVM runs that bytecode on any computer. That is why Java is \"platform independent\".", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>HelloWorld.java  --javac--&gt;  HelloWorld.class (bytecode)  --java--&gt;  JVM runs it\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Compiler:</strong> translates source code into a lower-level form. Java compiles to <strong>bytecode</strong>, a compact, platform-independent instruction set.</li>\n<li><strong>JVM (Java Virtual Machine):</strong> runs bytecode. Each operating system has its own JVM, so the same bytecode runs everywhere.</li>\n<li><strong>JRE (Java Runtime Environment):</strong> what you need to <em>run</em> Java programs. It sits between the program and the OS.</li>\n<li><strong>JDK (Java Development Kit):</strong> tools to <em>build</em> and run Java programs, including <code>javac</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>API (Application Program Interface):</strong> the library of prewritten classes and methods you can use (like <code>Scanner</code> or <code>Math</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Java language specification:</strong> the official rules for how Java works.</li>\n<li><strong>Garbage collector:</strong> part of the JVM that frees memory used by objects nothing refers to any more.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compile and run from the command line</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>javac<span class=\"w\"> </span>HelloWorld.java<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\"># compile: creates HelloWorld.class</span>\njava<span class=\"w\"> </span>HelloWorld<span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"c1\"># run: no .class at the end</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "helloworld.java --javac--> helloworld.class (bytecode) --java--> jvm runs it compiler: translates source code into a lower-level form. java compiles to bytecode , a compact, platform-independent instruction set. jvm (java virtual machine): runs bytecode. each operating system has its own jvm, so the same bytecode runs everywhere. jre (java runtime environment): what you need to run java programs. it sits between the program and the os. jdk (java development kit): tools to build and run java programs, including javac . api (application program interface): the library of prewritten classes and methods you can use (like scanner or math ). java language specification: the official rules for how java works. garbage collector: part of the jvm that frees memory used by objects nothing refers to any more. compile and run from the command line javac helloworld.java # compile: creates helloworld.class java helloworld # run: no .class at the end"}, {"id": "program-structure", "title": "Program structure and syntax", "src": "Ch. 1, Ch. 2", "idea": "Every program lives in a class, and it starts running at the main method. The public class name must match the file name, and Java is case sensitive.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">HelloWorld</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello, Java!\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>public class HelloWorld</code> defines a class named HelloWorld.</li>\n<li><code>public static void main(String[] args)</code> is the <strong>main method</strong>, where the program starts.</li>\n<li><code>System.out.println(...)</code> prints a line to the console. <code>System.out.print(...)</code> prints without a new line.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>File rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The file name must match the public class: <code>public class HelloWorld</code> is saved as <code>HelloWorld.java</code>.</li>\n<li>Compiling creates <code>HelloWorld.class</code>.</li>\n<li>Only one public class per file.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Syntax basics</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Java is <strong>case sensitive</strong>: <code>main</code>, <code>Main</code> and <code>MAIN</code> are different.</li>\n<li>Most statements end with a <strong>semicolon</strong> <code>;</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Braces</strong> <code>{ }</code> group code into blocks.</li>\n<li><strong>Keywords</strong> (reserved words) like <code>public</code>, <code>class</code>, <code>static</code>, <code>void</code> can't be used as names.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong> are ignored by the compiler:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">// line comment</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">/* block comment</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">   over several lines */</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Good style</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Indent consistently inside each block.</li>\n<li>Use meaningful names: <code>int studentAge;</code> instead of <code>int x;</code>.</li>\n<li>Comment where it helps, but don't over-comment obvious code.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>IDEs</strong> (IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, NetBeans, VS Code) help you write, compile, run and debug, and they highlight errors as you type.</p>", "text": "public class helloworld { public static void main ( string [] args ) { system . out . println ( \"hello, java!\" ); } } public class helloworld defines a class named helloworld. public static void main(string[] args) is the main method , where the program starts. system.out.println(...) prints a line to the console. system.out.print(...) prints without a new line. file rules the file name must match the public class: public class helloworld is saved as helloworld.java . compiling creates helloworld.class . only one public class per file. syntax basics java is case sensitive : main , main and main are different. most statements end with a semicolon ; . braces { } group code into blocks. keywords (reserved words) like public , class , static , void can't be used as names. comments are ignored by the compiler: // line comment /* block comment over several lines */ good style indent consistently inside each block. use meaningful names: int studentage; instead of int x; . comment where it helps, but don't over-comment obvious code. ides (intellij idea, eclipse, netbeans, vs code) help you write, compile, run and debug, and they highlight errors as you type."}, {"id": "errors", "title": "Three kinds of errors", "src": "Ch. 1, Ch. 2, Ch. 3", "idea": "Syntax errors break Java's grammar and the compiler catches them. Runtime errors happen while the program runs and can crash it. Logic errors run fine but give the wrong answer.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Error</th>\n<th>When it shows up</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Syntax</td>\n<td>At compile time</td>\n<td><code>System.out.println(\"Hello\")</code> (missing <code>;</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Runtime</td>\n<td>While running</td>\n<td><code>System.out.println(10 / 0);</code> (divide by zero)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Logic</td>\n<td>Never \"crashes\", just wrong</td>\n<td><code>int total = 10 - 5;</code> when you meant <code>+</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Common beginner errors</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting a semicolon: <code>int x = 5</code> → <code>int x = 5;</code></li>\n<li>Using a variable before giving it a value.</li>\n<li>Integer division: <code>5 / 2</code> is <code>2</code>, not <code>2.5</code>.</li>\n<li>Forgetting <code>import java.util.Scanner;</code></li>\n<li>Using <code>=</code> (assign) when you meant <code>==</code> (compare).</li>\n<li>Array index out of bounds.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Debugging techniques</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Print values with <code>System.out.println()</code> to trace what the program is doing.</li>\n<li>Check conditions, missing braces and wrong operators (<code>==</code> vs <code>=</code>).</li>\n<li>Test edge cases: 0, negative numbers, empty input, the first and last items.</li>\n<li>Use your IDE's debugger to step through line by line.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "error when it shows up example syntax at compile time system.out.println(\"hello\") (missing ; ) runtime while running system.out.println(10 / 0); (divide by zero) logic never \"crashes\", just wrong int total = 10 - 5; when you meant + common beginner errors forgetting a semicolon: int x = 5 → int x = 5; using a variable before giving it a value. integer division: 5 / 2 is 2 , not 2.5 . forgetting import java.util.scanner; using = (assign) when you meant == (compare). array index out of bounds. debugging techniques print values with system.out.println() to trace what the program is doing. check conditions, missing braces and wrong operators ( == vs = ). test edge cases: 0, negative numbers, empty input, the first and last items. use your ide's debugger to step through line by line."}, {"id": "variables", "title": "Variables, identifiers and constants", "src": "Ch. 2", "idea": "A variable is a named spot in memory that holds a value of one type. Give it a value before you use it, and use final for values that should never change.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">dataType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">variableName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">price</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">19.99</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Noah\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A variable must be assigned before it is used. <code>int x; System.out.println(x);</code> is a compile error.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Identifiers</strong> (names for variables, methods, classes, constants)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Can contain letters, digits, <code>_</code> and <code>$</code>.</li>\n<li>Can't start with a digit: <code>score1</code> is fine, <code>1score</code> is not.</li>\n<li>Can't be a reserved word: <code>int class;</code> is not allowed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Naming conventions</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>What</th>\n<th>Style</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Variables and methods</td>\n<td>camelCase</td>\n<td><code>studentAge</code>, <code>getBalance()</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Classes</td>\n<td>PascalCase</td>\n<td><code>LoanCalculator</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Constants</td>\n<td>ALL_CAPS</td>\n<td><code>MAX_SIZE</code>, <code>TAX_RATE</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Constants</strong> use <code>final</code>. Once assigned, the value can't change:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TAX_RATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.06</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MAX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">MAX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// compile error</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "datatype variablename = value ; int age = 20 ; double price = 19.99 ; string name = \"noah\" ; a variable must be assigned before it is used. int x; system.out.println(x); is a compile error. identifiers (names for variables, methods, classes, constants) can contain letters, digits, _ and $ . can't start with a digit: score1 is fine, 1score is not. can't be a reserved word: int class; is not allowed. naming conventions what style example variables and methods camelcase studentage , getbalance() classes pascalcase loancalculator constants all_caps max_size , tax_rate constants use final . once assigned, the value can't change: final double tax_rate = 0.06 ; final int max = 10 ; max = 20 ; // compile error"}, {"id": "data-types", "title": "Data types", "src": "Ch. 2, cheat sheet", "idea": "Primitive types hold simple values directly: whole numbers, decimals, single characters and true/false. String is a class, not a primitive, but you'll use it constantly.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n<th>Holds</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>byte</code></td>\n<td>8 bit</td>\n<td>very small integers</td>\n<td><code>byte b = 10;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>short</code></td>\n<td>16 bit</td>\n<td>small integers</td>\n<td><code>short s = 300;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>int</code></td>\n<td>32 bit</td>\n<td>most integers</td>\n<td><code>int age = 25;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>long</code></td>\n<td>64 bit</td>\n<td>very large integers</td>\n<td><code>long pop = 8000000000L;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>float</code></td>\n<td>32 bit</td>\n<td>decimals, less precise</td>\n<td><code>float t = 98.6F;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>double</code></td>\n<td>64 bit</td>\n<td>decimals, more precise</td>\n<td><code>double price = 19.99;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td>16 bit</td>\n<td>one Unicode character</td>\n<td><code>char grade = 'A';</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td><code>true</code> or <code>false</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean passed = true;</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>L</code> marks a long literal and the <code>F</code> marks a float literal.</li>\n<li>A <strong>literal</strong> is a value written directly in code: <code>100</code>, <code>12.5</code>, <code>'A'</code>, <code>\"hi\"</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Scientific notation:</strong> <code>1.23e4</code> means 1.23 × 10⁴ = <code>12300.0</code>.</li>\n<li>Other literal forms: hex <code>0x1AF</code>, binary <code>0b00101</code>.</li>\n<li><code>String</code> holds text and uses double quotes. <code>char</code> uses single quotes.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "type size holds example byte 8 bit very small integers byte b = 10; short 16 bit small integers short s = 300; int 32 bit most integers int age = 25; long 64 bit very large integers long pop = 8000000000l; float 32 bit decimals, less precise float t = 98.6f; double 64 bit decimals, more precise double price = 19.99; char 16 bit one unicode character char grade = 'a'; boolean — true or false boolean passed = true; the l marks a long literal and the f marks a float literal. a literal is a value written directly in code: 100 , 12.5 , 'a' , \"hi\" . scientific notation: 1.23e4 means 1.23 × 10⁴ = 12300.0 . other literal forms: hex 0x1af , binary 0b00101 . string holds text and uses double quotes. char uses single quotes."}, {"id": "operators", "title": "Operators and expressions", "src": "Ch. 2, Ch. 3", "idea": "Java does math with + - * / %, follows normal order of operations, and has shortcuts like += and ++. Watch out: dividing two ints drops the decimal.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operator</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th><code>10 ? 3</code> gives</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>+</code></td>\n<td>add</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>-</code></td>\n<td>subtract</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>*</code></td>\n<td>multiply</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/</code></td>\n<td>divide</td>\n<td>3 (integer division)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%</code></td>\n<td>remainder</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Integer division drops the decimal</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// 2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">5.0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// 2.5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Remainder <code>%</code></strong> is great for \"is it even?\" checks: <code>if (number % 2 == 0)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Exponents</strong> use a method, not an operator: <code>Math.pow(2, 3)</code> → <code>8.0</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Assignment</strong> <code>=</code> means \"store this value\", not \"equals\". <code>x = x + 1;</code> takes the old x, adds 1, and stores it back.</p>\n<p><strong>Order of operations:</strong> parentheses → <code>* / %</code> → <code>+ -</code>. So <code>2 + 3 * 4</code> is <code>14</code>, and <code>(2 + 3) * 4</code> is <code>20</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Augmented assignment</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Long way</th>\n<th>Shortcut</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>x = x + 5;</code></td>\n<td><code>x += 5;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>x = x - 5;</code></td>\n<td><code>x -= 5;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>x = x * 5;</code></td>\n<td><code>x *= 5;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>x = x / 5;</code></td>\n<td><code>x /= 5;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>x = x % 5;</code></td>\n<td><code>x %= 5;</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Increment and decrement:</strong> <code>x++</code> adds 1, <code>x--</code> subtracts 1.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// post: y gets 5, then x becomes 6</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// pre: a becomes 6, then b gets 6</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Precedence (high to low):</strong> <code>()</code> → unary <code>! ++ --</code> → <code>* / %</code> → <code>+ -</code> → relational <code>&lt; &gt; &lt;= &gt;=</code> → <code>== !=</code> → <code>&amp;&amp;</code> → <code>||</code> → <code>?:</code> → assignment <code>=</code>. Most operators group left to right. Assignment groups right to left.</p>", "text": "operator meaning 10 ? 3 gives + add 13 - subtract 7 * multiply 30 / divide 3 (integer division) % remainder 1 integer division drops the decimal system . out . println ( 5 / 2 ); // 2 system . out . println ( 5.0 / 2 ); // 2.5 remainder % is great for \"is it even?\" checks: if (number % 2 == 0) . exponents use a method, not an operator: math.pow(2, 3) → 8.0 . assignment = means \"store this value\", not \"equals\". x = x + 1; takes the old x, adds 1, and stores it back. order of operations: parentheses → * / % → + - . so 2 + 3 * 4 is 14 , and (2 + 3) * 4 is 20 . augmented assignment long way shortcut x = x + 5; x += 5; x = x - 5; x -= 5; x = x * 5; x *= 5; x = x / 5; x /= 5; x = x % 5; x %= 5; increment and decrement: x++ adds 1, x-- subtracts 1. int x = 5 ; int y = x ++ ; // post: y gets 5, then x becomes 6 int a = 5 ; int b = ++ a ; // pre: a becomes 6, then b gets 6 precedence (high to low): () → unary ! ++ -- → * / % → + - → relational < > <= >= → == != → && → || → ?: → assignment = . most operators group left to right. assignment groups right to left."}, {"id": "casting", "title": "Casting, conversion and overflow", "src": "Ch. 2, cheat sheet", "idea": "Casting converts one type to another. Small-to-large (widening) happens on its own. Large-to-small (narrowing) needs an explicit cast and cuts off the decimal.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">9.7</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 9 (decimal cut off, not rounded)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// 10.0 (widening, automatic)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Widening:</strong> smaller type to larger type (<code>int</code> → <code>double</code>). Automatic.</li>\n<li><strong>Narrowing:</strong> larger type to smaller (<code>double</code> → <code>int</code>). You must write the cast.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Converting text to numbers</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">parseInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"123\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Double</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">parseDouble</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"1.5\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fromHex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">parseInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"7A\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 122</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">toString</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">99</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"63\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Overflow:</strong> a value too big for its type wraps around to the other end.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2147483647</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// Integer.MAX_VALUE</span>\n<span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// -2147483648</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Underflow:</strong> a floating-point value gets too close to zero for the type to represent.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "double x = 9.7 ; int y = ( int ) x ; // 9 (decimal cut off, not rounded) int a = 10 ; double b = a ; // 10.0 (widening, automatic) widening: smaller type to larger type ( int → double ). automatic. narrowing: larger type to smaller ( double → int ). you must write the cast. converting text to numbers int n = integer . parseint ( \"123\" ); double d = double . parsedouble ( \"1.5\" ); int fromhex = integer . parseint ( \"7a\" , 16 ); // 122 string hex = integer . tostring ( 99 , 16 ); // \"63\" overflow: a value too big for its type wraps around to the other end. int x = 2147483647 ; // integer.max_value x = x + 1 ; system . out . println ( x ); // -2147483648 underflow: a floating-point value gets too close to zero for the type to represent."}, {"id": "scanner-input", "title": "Keyboard input with Scanner", "src": "Ch. 2, Ch. 4, learning plan", "idea": "Scanner reads what the user types. Import it, create one connected to System.in, then call a method that matches the type you want to read.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">InputExample</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">in</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Enter your age: \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"You are \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" years old.\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Reads</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextInt()</code></td>\n<td>an int</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextDouble()</code></td>\n<td>a double</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextLong()</code>, <code>nextFloat()</code>, <code>nextShort()</code>, <code>nextByte()</code></td>\n<td>that type</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>next()</code></td>\n<td>one word (stops at whitespace)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextLine()</code></td>\n<td>the whole line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hasNextInt()</code>, <code>hasNext()</code></td>\n<td>checks what's coming without reading it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Reading one character:</strong> there's no <code>nextChar()</code>. Use <code>input.next().charAt(0)</code>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> after <code>nextInt()</code> or <code>nextDouble()</code>, the Enter key is still waiting in the input. A <code>nextLine()</code> right after will read that empty leftover. Call an extra <code>input.nextLine();</code> first to clear it. <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Validating input</strong> so a typo doesn't crash the program:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Enter your age: \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hasNextInt</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Age cannot be negative.\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Please enter a whole number.\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">next</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// throw away the bad input</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Imports:</strong> <code>import java.util.Scanner;</code> brings in one class. <code>import java.util.*;</code> brings in the whole package. Specific imports are usually cleaner.</p>", "text": "import java.util.scanner ; public class inputexample { public static void main ( string [] args ) { scanner input = new scanner ( system . in ); system . out . print ( \"enter your age: \" ); int age = input . nextint (); system . out . println ( \"you are \" + age + \" years old.\" ); } } method reads nextint() an int nextdouble() a double nextlong() , nextfloat() , nextshort() , nextbyte() that type next() one word (stops at whitespace) nextline() the whole line hasnextint() , hasnext() checks what's coming without reading it reading one character: there's no nextchar() . use input.next().charat(0) . heads up: after nextint() or nextdouble() , the enter key is still waiting in the input. a nextline() right after will read that empty leftover. call an extra input.nextline(); first to clear it. added by fern validating input so a typo doesn't crash the program: int age ; while ( true ) { system . out . print ( \"enter your age: \" ); if ( input . hasnextint ()) { age = input . nextint (); if ( age >= 0 ) break ; system . out . println ( \"age cannot be negative.\" ); } else { system . out . println ( \"please enter a whole number.\" ); input . next (); // throw away the bad input } } imports: import java.util.scanner; brings in one class. import java.util.*; brings in the whole package. specific imports are usually cleaner."}, {"id": "planning-programs", "title": "Planning a program", "src": "Ch. 2", "idea": "Before coding, work out the input, the processing and the output. Write the steps in plain English (pseudocode), then build and test one small piece at a time.", "deep": "<p><strong>IPO model</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Part</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Circle area example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Input</td>\n<td>data the program receives</td>\n<td>radius</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process</td>\n<td>what it does with the data</td>\n<td>area = radius × radius × π</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Output</td>\n<td>the result</td>\n<td>area</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Software development steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Requirements specification: what must the program do?</li>\n<li>System analysis: identify input, process and output.</li>\n<li>System design: plan the steps (pseudocode or an algorithm).</li>\n<li>Implementation: write the code.</li>\n<li>Testing: run it and check results.</li>\n<li>Debugging: fix problems.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Pseudocode</strong> is a plain-English plan:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>Ask the user for a radius\nRead the radius\nCalculate the area\nDisplay the area\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Incremental coding:</strong> write the input code and test it, add the calculation and test it, add the output and test it. Bugs are much easier to find this way.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">CircleArea</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">in</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">3.14159</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Enter a radius: \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextDouble</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">area</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PI</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"The area is \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">area</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Example: breaking cents into coins</strong> (uses <code>/</code> and <code>%</code> together)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dollars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quarters</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">25</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">25</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dimes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nickels</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pennies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>System.currentTimeMillis()</code> returns milliseconds since January 1, 1970 (the UNIX epoch). Handy for timing code.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "ipo model part meaning circle area example input data the program receives radius process what it does with the data area = radius × radius × π output the result area software development steps requirements specification: what must the program do? system analysis: identify input, process and output. system design: plan the steps (pseudocode or an algorithm). implementation: write the code. testing: run it and check results. debugging: fix problems. pseudocode is a plain-english plan: ask the user for a radius read the radius calculate the area display the area incremental coding: write the input code and test it, add the calculation and test it, add the output and test it. bugs are much easier to find this way. import java.util.scanner ; public class circlearea { public static void main ( string [] args ) { scanner input = new scanner ( system . in ); final double pi = 3.14159 ; system . out . print ( \"enter a radius: \" ); double radius = input . nextdouble (); double area = radius * radius * pi ; system . out . println ( \"the area is \" + area ); } } example: breaking cents into coins (uses / and % together) int dollars = cents / 100 ; cents = cents % 100 ; int quarters = cents / 25 ; cents = cents % 25 ; int dimes = cents / 10 ; cents = cents % 10 ; int nickels = cents / 5 ; int pennies = cents % 5 ; system.currenttimemillis() returns milliseconds since january 1, 1970 (the unix epoch). handy for timing code."}]}, {"id": "control-flow", "title": "Decisions and loops", "blurb": "Choosing between paths with if and switch, and repeating work with loops.", "topics": [{"id": "booleans", "title": "Booleans and logical operators", "src": "Ch. 3", "idea": "Every decision in Java comes down to true or false. Relational operators compare values, and logical operators (&&, ||, !) combine those comparisons.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">boolean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isValid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// true</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Relational operators</strong> (each returns a boolean): <code>&lt;</code> <code>&lt;=</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>&gt;=</code> <code>==</code> <code>!=</code></p>\n<p><strong>Logical operators</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operator</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>True when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&amp;&amp;</code></td>\n<td>AND</td>\n<td>both sides are true</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>||</code></td>\n<td>OR</td>\n<td>at least one side is true</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>!</code></td>\n<td>NOT</td>\n<td>flips true and false</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>^</code></td>\n<td>XOR</td>\n<td>exactly one side is true</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">18</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hasLicense</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Can drive\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Short-circuit evaluation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&amp;&amp;</code> stops as soon as the left side is false.</li>\n<li><code>||</code> stops as soon as the left side is true.</li>\n<li>This lets you guard risky checks:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// never divides by zero</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Example: leap year</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">year</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">year</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">year</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">400</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Leap year\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "boolean isvalid = true ; int x = 5 ; system . out . println ( x > 3 ); // true relational operators (each returns a boolean): < <= > >= == != logical operators operator meaning true when && and both sides are true || or at least one side is true ! not flips true and false ^ xor exactly one side is true if ( age > 18 && haslicense ) { system . out . println ( \"can drive\" ); } short-circuit evaluation && stops as soon as the left side is false. || stops as soon as the left side is true. this lets you guard risky checks: if ( x != 0 && 10 / x > 1 ) { // never divides by zero } example: leap year if (( year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0 ) || year % 400 == 0 ) { system . out . println ( \"leap year\" ); }"}, {"id": "if-statements", "title": "if, else if and else", "src": "Ch. 3, learning plan", "idea": "An if runs code only when its condition is true. Add else for a second path, or chain else if for several. Always use braces so it's clear which else belongs to which if.", "deep": "<p><strong>One-way</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Positive number\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Two-way</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Positive\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Not positive\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Multi-way</strong> (checks top to bottom and stops at the first true one)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">score</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">90</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">score</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">80</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"B\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">score</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">70</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"C\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Needs improvement\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Nested if</strong> puts an if inside another one.</p>\n<p><strong>Dangling else:</strong> without braces, an <code>else</code> attaches to the <em>nearest</em> <code>if</code>, which may not be the one you meant.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Big\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Small\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// belongs to the inner if!</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Typical programs to practice: BMI calculator, tax calculator, quiz, lottery, leap year checker.</p>", "text": "one-way if ( x > 0 ) { system . out . println ( \"positive number\" ); } two-way if ( x > 0 ) { system . out . println ( \"positive\" ); } else { system . out . println ( \"not positive\" ); } multi-way (checks top to bottom and stops at the first true one) if ( score >= 90 ) { system . out . println ( \"a\" ); } else if ( score >= 80 ) { system . out . println ( \"b\" ); } else if ( score >= 70 ) { system . out . println ( \"c\" ); } else { system . out . println ( \"needs improvement\" ); } nested if puts an if inside another one. dangling else: without braces, an else attaches to the nearest if , which may not be the one you meant. if ( x > 0 ) if ( x > 10 ) system . out . println ( \"big\" ); else system . out . println ( \"small\" ); // belongs to the inner if! typical programs to practice: bmi calculator, tax calculator, quiz, lottery, leap year checker."}, {"id": "switch-ternary", "title": "switch and the conditional operator", "src": "Ch. 3", "idea": "switch picks a branch by matching one value against fixed cases. The conditional operator ( ? : ) is a one-line if-else that produces a value.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">switch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">day</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Monday\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Tuesday\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">default</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Other day\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>break</code> ends the switch. Without it, the code <strong>falls through</strong> into the next case.</li>\n<li><code>default</code> runs when no case matches.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Newer arrow syntax</strong> (Java 14+, works in your Java 21) has no fall-through, so no <code>break</code> needed: <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">switch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">day</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Monday\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Tuesday\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Other day\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">};</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Conditional (ternary) operator</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// condition ? valueIfTrue : valueIfFalse</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "switch ( day ) { case 1 : system . out . println ( \"monday\" ); break ; case 2 : system . out . println ( \"tuesday\" ); break ; default : system . out . println ( \"other day\" ); } break ends the switch. without it, the code falls through into the next case. default runs when no case matches. newer arrow syntax (java 14+, works in your java 21) has no fall-through, so no break needed: added by fern string name = switch ( day ) { case 1 -> \"monday\" ; case 2 -> \"tuesday\" ; default -> \"other day\" ; }; conditional (ternary) operator int max = ( a > b ) ? a : b ; // condition ? valueiftrue : valueiffalse"}, {"id": "random-numbers", "title": "Random numbers", "src": "Ch. 3, Ch. 9", "idea": "Math.random() gives a double from 0.0 up to (not including) 1.0. Multiply and cast it to get a whole number in a range, or use the Random class.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">random</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"c1\">// 0.0 to &lt;1.0</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// 0 to 9</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">die</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 1 to 6</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>General formula:</strong> <code>(int) (Math.random() * count) + start</code></p>\n<p><strong>The Random class</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.Random</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Random</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Random</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rand</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 0 to 9</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "double r = math . random (); // 0.0 to <1.0 int num = ( int ) ( math . random () * 10 ); // 0 to 9 int die = ( int ) ( math . random () * 6 ) + 1 ; // 1 to 6 general formula: (int) (math.random() * count) + start the random class import java.util.random ; random rand = new random (); int n = rand . nextint ( 10 ); // 0 to 9"}, {"id": "while-loops", "title": "while and do-while loops", "src": "Ch. 5, learning plan", "idea": "A while loop repeats as long as its condition is true and checks before each pass. A do-while checks after, so its body always runs at least once.", "deep": "<p><strong>while</strong> (pretest loop: condition checked first)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>do-while</strong> (posttest loop: body runs, then the condition is checked)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// note the semicolon</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Sentinel value:</strong> a special input that means \"stop\".</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// -1 is the sentinel</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Designing a loop</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>What code repeats?</li>\n<li>When should it stop?</li>\n<li>What changes each pass so it eventually stops?</li>\n</ol>", "text": "while (pretest loop: condition checked first) int count = 1 ; while ( count <= 5 ) { system . out . println ( count ); count ++ ; } do-while (posttest loop: body runs, then the condition is checked) int number = 1 ; do { system . out . println ( number ); number ++ ; } while ( number <= 5 ); // note the semicolon sentinel value: a special input that means \"stop\". int number = input . nextint (); int sum = 0 ; while ( number != - 1 ) { // -1 is the sentinel sum += number ; number = input . nextint (); } designing a loop what code repeats? when should it stop? what changes each pass so it eventually stops?"}, {"id": "for-loops", "title": "for loops", "src": "Ch. 5", "idea": "A for loop packs the start value, the condition and the update into one line. Use it when you know how many times to repeat.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Part</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n<th>Here</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>initialization</td>\n<td>starting value, runs once</td>\n<td><code>int i = 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>condition</td>\n<td>checked before each pass</td>\n<td><code>i &lt;= 5</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>update</td>\n<td>runs after each pass</td>\n<td><code>i++</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Order each pass: condition → body → update → back to condition.</p>\n<p><strong>Choosing a loop</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Loop</th>\n<th>Condition checked</th>\n<th>Best for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>while</code></td>\n<td>before</td>\n<td>unknown number of repeats</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>do-while</code></td>\n<td>after</td>\n<td>must run at least once (menus, input prompts)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>for</code></td>\n<td>before</td>\n<td>known number of repeats</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "for ( int i = 1 ; i <= 5 ; i ++ ) { system . out . println ( i ); } part purpose here initialization starting value, runs once int i = 1 condition checked before each pass i <= 5 update runs after each pass i++ order each pass: condition → body → update → back to condition. choosing a loop loop condition checked best for while before unknown number of repeats do-while after must run at least once (menus, input prompts) for before known number of repeats"}, {"id": "loop-control", "title": "break, continue and nested loops", "src": "Ch. 5", "idea": "break leaves the loop immediately and continue skips to the next pass. A nested loop runs the whole inner loop once for every pass of the outer loop.", "deep": "<p><strong>break</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 1 2 3 4</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>continue</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">continue</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 1 2 4 5</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Nested loops:</strong> the outer loop usually controls rows and the inner loop controls columns.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"* \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// * * *</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// * * *</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// * * *</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "break for ( int i = 1 ; i <= 10 ; i ++ ) { if ( i == 5 ) break ; system . out . println ( i ); // 1 2 3 4 } continue for ( int i = 1 ; i <= 5 ; i ++ ) { if ( i == 3 ) continue ; system . out . println ( i ); // 1 2 4 5 } nested loops: the outer loop usually controls rows and the inner loop controls columns. for ( int row = 1 ; row <= 3 ; row ++ ) { for ( int col = 1 ; col <= 3 ; col ++ ) { system . out . print ( \"* \" ); } system . out . println (); } // * * * // * * * // * * *"}, {"id": "loop-pitfalls", "title": "Loop pitfalls", "src": "Ch. 5", "idea": "The big three loop bugs are infinite loops (nothing changes, so it never stops), off-by-one errors (one pass too many or too few) and comparing decimals for exact equality.", "deep": "<p><strong>Infinite loop:</strong> the condition never becomes false.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// i never changes!</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Common causes: forgetting to update the control variable, or a condition that's always true.</p>\n<p><strong>Off-by-one error</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// runs 4 times</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// runs 5 times</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Floating-point numbers aren't exact:</strong> <code>0.1 + 0.2</code> is not exactly <code>0.3</code>. Don't use <code>==</code> with doubles. Check that the difference is tiny instead:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">abs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1e-9</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cm\">/* close enough */</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Tracing:</strong> to understand a loop, write a small table of each variable's value on every pass.</p>", "text": "infinite loop: the condition never becomes false. int i = 1 ; while ( i <= 5 ) { system . out . println ( i ); // i never changes! } common causes: forgetting to update the control variable, or a condition that's always true. off-by-one error for ( int i = 1 ; i < 5 ; i ++ ) // runs 4 times for ( int i = 1 ; i <= 5 ; i ++ ) // runs 5 times floating-point numbers aren't exact: 0.1 + 0.2 is not exactly 0.3 . don't use == with doubles. check that the difference is tiny instead: if ( math . abs ( a - b ) < 1e-9 ) { /* close enough */ } tracing: to understand a loop, write a small table of each variable's value on every pass."}, {"id": "loop-problems", "title": "Classic loop problems", "src": "Ch. 5", "idea": "Two patterns you should be able to write from scratch: checking whether a number is prime, and checking whether a word is a palindrome.", "deep": "<p><strong>Prime numbers</strong> are greater than 1 and divisible only by 1 and themselves (2, 3, 5, 7…).</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">boolean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">prime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> you only need to test divisors up to the square root (<code>i * i &lt;= number</code>), and you can <code>break</code> at the first one you find. Your notes' version (<code>i &lt; number</code>) is also correct, just slower. <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Palindromes</strong> read the same both ways (\"racecar\", \"level\"). Compare characters from both ends, moving inward:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"level\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">boolean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isPalindrome</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">charAt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">charAt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">isPalindrome</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "prime numbers are greater than 1 and divisible only by 1 and themselves (2, 3, 5, 7…). boolean prime = number > 1 ; for ( int i = 2 ; i * i <= number ; i ++ ) { if ( number % i == 0 ) { prime = false ; break ; } } tip: you only need to test divisors up to the square root ( i * i <= number ), and you can break at the first one you find. your notes' version ( i < number ) is also correct, just slower. added by fern palindromes read the same both ways (\"racecar\", \"level\"). compare characters from both ends, moving inward: string word = \"level\" ; boolean ispalindrome = true ; int low = 0 , high = word . length () - 1 ; while ( low < high ) { if ( word . charat ( low ) != word . charat ( high )) { ispalindrome = false ; break ; } low ++ ; high -- ; }"}]}, {"id": "strings-math", "title": "Strings, characters and Math", "blurb": "Built-in math, single characters, text and formatting.", "topics": [{"id": "math-class", "title": "The Math class", "src": "Ch. 4", "idea": "Math is a class full of static methods for calculations: powers, roots, rounding, min and max, random numbers and trigonometry. You call them on the class itself, like Math.sqrt(25).", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.pow(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>a to the power b</td>\n<td><code>Math.pow(2, 3)</code> → <code>8.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.sqrt(x)</code></td>\n<td>square root</td>\n<td><code>Math.sqrt(25)</code> → <code>5.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.abs(x)</code></td>\n<td>absolute value</td>\n<td><code>Math.abs(-4)</code> → <code>4</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.max(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>larger</td>\n<td><code>Math.max(3, 7)</code> → <code>7</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.min(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>smaller</td>\n<td><code>Math.min(3, 7)</code> → <code>3</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.round(x)</code></td>\n<td>nearest whole number</td>\n<td><code>Math.round(4.6)</code> → <code>5</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.ceil(x)</code></td>\n<td>round up</td>\n<td><code>Math.ceil(4.2)</code> → <code>5.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.floor(x)</code></td>\n<td>round down</td>\n<td><code>Math.floor(4.9)</code> → <code>4.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.random()</code></td>\n<td>0.0 to &lt;1.0</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.log(x)</code></td>\n<td>natural log</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> <code>sqrt</code>, <code>ceil</code>, <code>floor</code> and <code>pow</code> return a <strong>double</strong>, so you'll see <code>5.0</code>, not <code>5</code>. <span class=\"by\">Fixed from the original notes</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Trigonometry</strong> works in radians:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">angle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">toRadians</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">90</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sin</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">angle</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 1.0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Also: <code>cos()</code>, <code>tan()</code>, <code>toDegrees()</code>, and the constant <code>Math.PI</code>.</p>", "text": "method does example math.pow(a, b) a to the power b math.pow(2, 3) → 8.0 math.sqrt(x) square root math.sqrt(25) → 5.0 math.abs(x) absolute value math.abs(-4) → 4 math.max(a, b) larger math.max(3, 7) → 7 math.min(a, b) smaller math.min(3, 7) → 3 math.round(x) nearest whole number math.round(4.6) → 5 math.ceil(x) round up math.ceil(4.2) → 5.0 math.floor(x) round down math.floor(4.9) → 4.0 math.random() 0.0 to <1.0 — math.log(x) natural log — heads up: sqrt , ceil , floor and pow return a double , so you'll see 5.0 , not 5 . fixed from the original notes trigonometry works in radians: double angle = math . toradians ( 90 ); system . out . println ( math . sin ( angle )); // 1.0 also: cos() , tan() , todegrees() , and the constant math.pi ."}, {"id": "chars-unicode", "title": "Characters and Unicode", "src": "Ch. 4", "idea": "A char holds one character in single quotes. Under the hood every character is a number (its Unicode value), so you can convert between char and int.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">letter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">digit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'7'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// strings use double quotes</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ASCII:</strong> older encoding, values 0–127. <code>'A'</code> is 65, <code>'a'</code> is 97.</li>\n<li><strong>Unicode:</strong> the modern system covering many languages and symbols. Java's <code>char</code> uses Unicode.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>char ↔ int</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ch</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"c1\">// 65</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">66</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// 'B'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>The Character class</strong> (static helper methods)</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isDigit(ch)</code></td>\n<td>is it 0–9?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isLetter(ch)</code></td>\n<td>is it a letter?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isLetterOrDigit(ch)</code></td>\n<td>either</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isUpperCase(ch)</code> / <code>isLowerCase(ch)</code></td>\n<td>case check</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.toUpperCase(ch)</code> / <code>toLowerCase(ch)</code></td>\n<td>convert case</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Example: hex character to its decimal value</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'F'</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'A'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 10</span>\n<span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'0'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Hex to decimal by hand:</strong> hex digits are 0–9 and A–F (A=10 … F=15). <code>2F</code> = 2 × 16¹ + 15 × 16⁰ = 32 + 15 = <strong>47</strong>.</p>", "text": "char letter = 'a' ; char digit = '7' ; string word = \"hello\" ; // strings use double quotes ascii: older encoding, values 0–127. 'a' is 65, 'a' is 97. unicode: the modern system covering many languages and symbols. java's char uses unicode. char ↔ int char ch = 'a' ; int code = ch ; // 65 char next = ( char ) 66 ; // 'b' the character class (static helper methods) method does character.isdigit(ch) is it 0–9? character.isletter(ch) is it a letter? character.isletterordigit(ch) either character.isuppercase(ch) / islowercase(ch) case check character.touppercase(ch) / tolowercase(ch) convert case example: hex character to its decimal value char hex = 'a' ; int value ; if ( hex >= 'a' && hex <= 'f' ) value = hex - 'a' + 10 ; // 10 else value = hex - '0' ; hex to decimal by hand: hex digits are 0–9 and a–f (a=10 … f=15). 2f = 2 × 16¹ + 15 × 16⁰ = 32 + 15 = 47 ."}, {"id": "escape-sequences", "title": "Escape sequences", "src": "Ch. 4", "idea": "A backslash inside a string starts an escape sequence, a code for a character you can't type directly, like a new line or a quote mark.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Sequence</th>\n<th>Means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\n</code></td>\n<td>new line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\t</code></td>\n<td>tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\\\</code></td>\n<td>backslash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\\"</code></td>\n<td>double quote</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\'</code></td>\n<td>single quote</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello\\nWorld\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// Hello</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">// World</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Whitespace characters:</strong> space, tab <code>\\t</code>, newline <code>\\n</code>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "sequence means \\n new line \\t tab \\\\ backslash \\\" double quote \\' single quote system . out . println ( \"hello\\nworld\" ); // hello // world whitespace characters: space, tab \\t , newline \\n ."}, {"id": "strings", "title": "Working with Strings", "src": "Ch. 4, cheat sheet", "idea": "A String is an object holding a sequence of characters. Positions (indexes) start at 0, and you work with strings through methods like length(), charAt() and substring().", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Java\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">//  J  a  v  a</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">//  0  1  2  3</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">());</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// 4</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">charAt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// v</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Instance vs static methods:</strong> <code>word.length()</code> is an <em>instance</em> method (called on an object). <code>Math.sqrt(25)</code> is a <em>static</em> method (called on the class).</p>\n<p><strong>Joining strings</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">full</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">joined</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">concat</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Common methods</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>length()</code></td>\n<td>number of characters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>charAt(i)</code></td>\n<td>the char at index i</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>substring(begin, end)</code></td>\n<td>part of the string (end <strong>not</strong> included)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>substring(begin)</code></td>\n<td>from begin to the end</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>indexOf(\"x\")</code></td>\n<td>first position, or -1 if not found</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>indexOf(\"x\", start)</code></td>\n<td>search starting at start</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>contains(\"x\")</code></td>\n<td>true/false</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>startsWith(\"x\")</code> / <code>endsWith(\"x\")</code></td>\n<td>true/false</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>toUpperCase()</code> / <code>toLowerCase()</code></td>\n<td>changed copy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>trim()</code></td>\n<td>copy without spaces at both ends</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>replace(old, new)</code></td>\n<td>copy with replacements</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>split(\" \")</code></td>\n<td>array of pieces</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>equals(other)</code> / <code>equalsIgnoreCase(other)</code></td>\n<td>same contents?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>compareTo(other)</code></td>\n<td>alphabetical comparison</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Programming\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">substring</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"Program\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">indexOf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"g\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// 3</span>\n<span class=\"s\">\"   hi   \"</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">trim</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"hi\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "string word = \"java\" ; // j a v a // 0 1 2 3 system . out . println ( word . length ()); // 4 system . out . println ( word . charat ( 2 )); // v instance vs static methods: word.length() is an instance method (called on an object). math.sqrt(25) is a static method (called on the class). joining strings string full = first + \" \" + second ; string joined = first . concat ( second ); common methods method returns length() number of characters charat(i) the char at index i substring(begin, end) part of the string (end not included) substring(begin) from begin to the end indexof(\"x\") first position, or -1 if not found indexof(\"x\", start) search starting at start contains(\"x\") true/false startswith(\"x\") / endswith(\"x\") true/false touppercase() / tolowercase() changed copy trim() copy without spaces at both ends replace(old, new) copy with replacements split(\" \") array of pieces equals(other) / equalsignorecase(other) same contents? compareto(other) alphabetical comparison string text = \"programming\" ; text . substring ( 0 , 7 ); // \"program\" text . indexof ( \"g\" ); // 3 \" hi \" . trim (); // \"hi\""}, {"id": "comparing-strings", "title": "Comparing strings", "src": "Ch. 4", "idea": "Use equals() to check whether two strings have the same characters. == only checks whether they are the exact same object in memory, which is usually not what you want.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Java\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Java\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">s1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">equals</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// true: same contents</span>\n<span class=\"n\">s1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s2</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// compares references (memory locations)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> <code>==</code> on strings sometimes <em>seems</em> to work because of the string pool, then fails with strings read from input. Always use <code>equals()</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>compareTo()</strong> compares alphabetically (by Unicode values):</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"s\">\"Apple\"</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">compareTo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Banana\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// negative</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Result</th>\n<th>Means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>negative</td>\n<td>first comes before second</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>positive</td>\n<td>first comes after second</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "string s1 = \"java\" ; string s2 = \"java\" ; s1 . equals ( s2 ); // true: same contents s1 == s2 ; // compares references (memory locations) heads up: == on strings sometimes seems to work because of the string pool, then fails with strings read from input. always use equals() . compareto() compares alphabetically (by unicode values): \"apple\" . compareto ( \"banana\" ); // negative result means 0 equal negative first comes before second positive first comes after second"}, {"id": "formatting", "title": "printf and text blocks", "src": "Ch. 4", "idea": "printf prints with placeholders (format specifiers) like %d and %.2f, so you control decimals and alignment. Text blocks (\"\"\") let you write multi-line strings.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Specifier</th>\n<th>For</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%d</code></td>\n<td>integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%f</code></td>\n<td>decimal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%.2f</code></td>\n<td>decimal with 2 places</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%s</code></td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%c</code></td>\n<td>character</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%n</code></td>\n<td>new line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%10s</code>, <code>%-10s</code></td>\n<td>width 10, right or left aligned</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">price</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">19.999</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"%.2f%n\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">price</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"c1\">// 20.00</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"%s is %d%n\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Noah\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">format</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"%.1f\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">3.14159</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"3.1\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Text blocks</strong> (multi-line strings):</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"\"\"</span>\n<span class=\"s\">    Hello</span>\n<span class=\"s\">    Welcome to Java</span>\n<span class=\"s\">    \"\"\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "specifier for %d integer %f decimal %.2f decimal with 2 places %s string %c character %n new line %10s , %-10s width 10, right or left aligned double price = 19.999 ; system . out . printf ( \"%.2f%n\" , price ); // 20.00 system . out . printf ( \"%s is %d%n\" , \"noah\" , 20 ); string s = string . format ( \"%.1f\" , 3.14159 ); // \"3.1\" text blocks (multi-line strings): string message = \"\"\" hello welcome to java \"\"\" ;"}, {"id": "stringbuilder", "title": "String immutability and StringBuilder", "src": "Ch. 10, cheat sheet", "idea": "Strings can never change after they're created: every \"change\" makes a new String. When you build up text in a loop, use StringBuilder, which changes in place and is much faster.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" world\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// creates a brand-new String object</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Strings are <strong>immutable</strong> and stored in a shared area called the <strong>string pool</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>StringBuilder</strong> is a mutable string:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">StringBuilder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StringBuilder</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">append</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\" World\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">insert</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"&gt;&gt; \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">reverse</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">toString</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Class</th>\n<th>Thread-safe</th>\n<th>Speed</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>StringBuilder</code></td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Faster</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>StringBuffer</code></td>\n<td>Yes (synchronized)</td>\n<td>Slower</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Use <code>StringBuilder</code> unless several threads share the same object.</p>", "text": "string s = \"hello\" ; s = s + \" world\" ; // creates a brand-new string object strings are immutable and stored in a shared area called the string pool . stringbuilder is a mutable string: stringbuilder sb = new stringbuilder ( \"hello\" ); sb . append ( \" world\" ); sb . insert ( 0 , \">> \" ); sb . reverse (); string result = sb . tostring (); class thread-safe speed stringbuilder no faster stringbuffer yes (synchronized) slower use stringbuilder unless several threads share the same object."}]}, {"id": "methods", "title": "Methods", "blurb": "Packaging code into reusable, named pieces.", "topics": [{"id": "method-basics", "title": "Method anatomy", "src": "Ch. 6, learning plan", "idea": "A method is a named block of code that does one task. Its header says what goes in (parameters) and what comes out (the return type, or void for nothing).", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">modifier</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">returnType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">methodName</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">parameters</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// body</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Part</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>public</code></td>\n<td>access modifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>static</code></td>\n<td>belongs to the class, not an object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>int</code></td>\n<td>return type</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add</code></td>\n<td>method name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(int a, int b)</code></td>\n<td>parameters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>return a + b;</code></td>\n<td>sends a value back</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>void vs value-returning</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">greet</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"c1\">// void: does an action</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hi\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">multiply</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// returns a value</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A <code>void</code> method can use <code>return;</code> to exit early.</li>\n<li>A value-returning method must <code>return</code> on every path, or it won't compile.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Calling (invoking) a method:</strong> <code>int result = add(2, 3);</code> The caller pauses, the method runs, then control returns to the caller with the result.</p>\n<p><strong>Why use methods:</strong> organize code, avoid repetition, make debugging easier, improve readability.</p>", "text": "modifier returntype methodname ( parameters ) { // body } public static int add ( int a , int b ) { return a + b ; } part meaning public access modifier static belongs to the class, not an object int return type add method name (int a, int b) parameters return a + b; sends a value back void vs value-returning public static void greet () { // void: does an action system . out . println ( \"hi\" ); } public static int multiply ( int x , int y ) { // returns a value return x * y ; } a void method can use return; to exit early. a value-returning method must return on every path, or it won't compile. calling (invoking) a method: int result = add(2, 3); the caller pauses, the method runs, then control returns to the caller with the result. why use methods: organize code, avoid repetition, make debugging easier, improve readability."}, {"id": "parameters", "title": "Parameters and pass-by-value", "src": "Ch. 6, Ch. 7, Ch. 9", "idea": "Java always passes a copy of the value. For primitives, the method can't change your original variable. For objects and arrays, the copy is of the reference, so the method can change the object it points to.", "deep": "<ul>\n<li><strong>Formal parameter:</strong> the variable in the method header (<code>int number</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Actual parameter (argument):</strong> the value you pass in the call (<code>square(5)</code>).</li>\n<li>Arguments must match the parameters in number, order and type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Primitives: the original doesn't change</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">change</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Arrays and objects: the contents can change</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">change</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// changes the caller's array</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">changeCircle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// changes the caller's object</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> the arrays guide says arrays are \"passed by reference\". More precisely, Java is <strong>always</strong> pass-by-value, and for an array the value being copied is a <em>reference</em>. That's why the method can change the array's contents but can't make your variable point to a different array. <span class=\"by\">Clarified by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "formal parameter: the variable in the method header ( int number ). actual parameter (argument): the value you pass in the call ( square(5) ). arguments must match the parameters in number, order and type. primitives: the original doesn't change public static void change ( int x ) { x = 100 ; } int num = 5 ; change ( num ); system . out . println ( num ); // 5 arrays and objects: the contents can change public static void change ( int [] arr ) { arr [ 0 ] = 100 ; // changes the caller's array } public static void changecircle ( circle c ) { c . radius = 20 ; // changes the caller's object } heads up: the arrays guide says arrays are \"passed by reference\". more precisely, java is always pass-by-value, and for an array the value being copied is a reference . that's why the method can change the array's contents but can't make your variable point to a different array. clarified by fern"}, {"id": "overloading", "title": "Overloading and signatures", "src": "Ch. 6", "idea": "Overloading means several methods share a name but take different parameters. Java picks the one whose parameter list matches the call.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Overloads must differ in the <strong>number</strong> or <strong>types</strong> of parameters.</li>\n<li>You <strong>can't</strong> overload by return type alone:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// compile error</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Method signature</strong> = name + parameter list, like <code>sum(int, int)</code>. The return type is not part of it.</li>\n<li><strong>Ambiguous invocation:</strong> when two overloads match a call equally well, Java can't choose and it's a compile error.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public static int add ( int a , int b ) public static double add ( double a , double b ) public static int add ( int a , int b , int c ) overloads must differ in the number or types of parameters. you can't overload by return type alone: int test ( int x ) double test ( int x ) // compile error method signature = name + parameter list, like sum(int, int) . the return type is not part of it. ambiguous invocation: when two overloads match a call equally well, java can't choose and it's a compile error."}, {"id": "scope", "title": "Variable scope", "src": "Ch. 6, Ch. 9", "idea": "A variable only exists inside the block where it's declared, from its declaration to the closing brace. Outside that block it's gone.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// local to test()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// error: x doesn't exist here</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Kind</th>\n<th>Declared</th>\n<th>Visible</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Local</td>\n<td>inside a method or block</td>\n<td>from declaration to the closing <code>}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Instance</td>\n<td>in the class, no <code>static</code></td>\n<td>throughout the class, one per object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Static</td>\n<td>in the class with <code>static</code></td>\n<td>throughout the class, shared</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>A loop variable declared in <code>for (int i = 0; ...)</code> exists only inside that loop.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public static void test () { int x = 5 ; // local to test() } system . out . println ( x ); // error: x doesn't exist here kind declared visible local inside a method or block from declaration to the closing } instance in the class, no static throughout the class, one per object static in the class with static throughout the class, shared a loop variable declared in for (int i = 0; ...) exists only inside that loop."}, {"id": "method-design", "title": "Designing with methods", "src": "Ch. 6", "idea": "Break a big problem into smaller methods (stepwise refinement). You can then use each method without thinking about how it works inside (abstraction).", "deep": "<ul>\n<li><strong>Method abstraction:</strong> use a method without knowing its internals, like <code>Math.sqrt(25)</code>. This hides implementation details (<strong>information hiding</strong>, part of <strong>encapsulation</strong>).</li>\n<li><strong>Stepwise refinement / divide and conquer:</strong> solve the main problem by splitting it into smaller tasks, each its own method.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>main()\n ├── inputData()\n ├── processData()\n └── displayResults()\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Top-down design:</strong> start with the big picture and break it down.</li>\n<li><strong>Bottom-up design:</strong> build small methods first, then combine them.</li>\n<li><strong>Stub:</strong> an empty placeholder method you fill in later. It lets you test the overall structure early.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">calculate</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// TODO</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Benefits: easier debugging, easier maintenance, reusable code.</p>", "text": "method abstraction: use a method without knowing its internals, like math.sqrt(25) . this hides implementation details ( information hiding , part of encapsulation ). stepwise refinement / divide and conquer: solve the main problem by splitting it into smaller tasks, each its own method. main() ├── inputdata() ├── processdata() └── displayresults() top-down design: start with the big picture and break it down. bottom-up design: build small methods first, then combine them. stub: an empty placeholder method you fill in later. it lets you test the overall structure early. public static void calculate () { // todo } benefits: easier debugging, easier maintenance, reusable code."}, {"id": "recursion", "title": "Recursion", "src": "learning plan, cheat sheet", "idea": "A recursive method calls itself on a smaller version of the problem. It needs a base case that stops the calls, or it runs forever (and crashes with a StackOverflowError).", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">factorial</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"c1\">// base case</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">factorial</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// recursive call</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Tracing <code>factorial(4)</code></strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>4 × factorial(3)\n4 × 3 × factorial(2)\n4 × 3 × 2 × factorial(1)\n4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 24\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Every recursive method needs: (1) a base case that returns right away, and (2) a recursive case that moves toward the base case.</li>\n<li>Tracing calls on paper helps more than reading about it.</li>\n<li>Good first practice: factorial, sum of 1..n, reversing a string, counting digits.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public static int factorial ( int number ) { if ( number <= 1 ) { // base case return 1 ; } return number * factorial ( number - 1 ); // recursive call } tracing factorial(4) 4 × factorial(3) 4 × 3 × factorial(2) 4 × 3 × 2 × factorial(1) 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 24 every recursive method needs: (1) a base case that returns right away, and (2) a recursive case that moves toward the base case. tracing calls on paper helps more than reading about it. good first practice: factorial, sum of 1..n, reversing a string, counting digits."}]}, {"id": "arrays", "title": "Arrays", "blurb": "Storing many values of one type, plus searching, sorting and tables.", "topics": [{"id": "array-basics", "title": "Array basics", "src": "Ch. 7", "idea": "An array holds a fixed number of values of the same type under one name. You reach each value by its index, which runs from 0 to length - 1.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scores</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// 5 slots, indexes 0–4</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">};</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// initializer shortcut</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// 20</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// 3 (no parentheses!)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Declare</strong> <code>int[] numbers;</code> (preferred) or <code>int numbers[];</code> (legal, less common).</li>\n<li><strong>Create</strong> <code>numbers = new int[5];</code>. The size is fixed once created.</li>\n<li><strong>Why arrays:</strong> store lots of related data, loop over it, write shorter code. Most algorithms use them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Default values</strong> in a new array</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>int</code>, <code>long</code>, etc.</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>double</code></td>\n<td><code>0.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td><code>'\\u0000'</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td><code>false</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>String</code> and other objects</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Out of bounds:</strong> <code>nums[3]</code> on a 3-element array throws <code>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException</code>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> it's <code>arr.length</code> for arrays, but <code>str.length()</code> for strings and <code>list.size()</code> for lists.</p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "int [] scores = new int [ 5 ] ; // 5 slots, indexes 0–4 int [] nums = { 10 , 20 , 30 }; // initializer shortcut system . out . println ( nums [ 1 ] ); // 20 system . out . println ( nums . length ); // 3 (no parentheses!) declare int[] numbers; (preferred) or int numbers[]; (legal, less common). create numbers = new int[5]; . the size is fixed once created. why arrays: store lots of related data, loop over it, write shorter code. most algorithms use them. default values in a new array type default int , long , etc. 0 double 0.0 char '\\u0000' boolean false string and other objects null out of bounds: nums[3] on a 3-element array throws arrayindexoutofboundsexception . heads up: it's arr.length for arrays, but str.length() for strings and list.size() for lists."}, {"id": "array-operations", "title": "Common array operations", "src": "Ch. 7", "idea": "Most array work is a loop over every index: printing, summing, or finding the biggest or smallest value. A for-each loop is the simplest way to read every element.", "deep": "<p><strong>Standard loop</strong> (use <code>&lt;</code>, not <code>&lt;=</code>)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Sum</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Max</strong> (min is the same with <code>&lt;</code>)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Random shuffle</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">random</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">temp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">temp</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Shift left</strong> by one</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>For-each loop</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Regular <code>for</code></th>\n<th>For-each</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Uses an index</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Simpler syntax</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Can change elements</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No (assigning to <code>value</code> doesn't change the array)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Arrays model lots of things: a deck of cards (<code>String[] suits = {\"Hearts\", \"Spades\", \"Clubs\", \"Diamonds\"};</code>), scores to analyze, players.</p>", "text": "standard loop (use < , not <= ) for ( int i = 0 ; i < nums . length ; i ++ ) { system . out . print ( nums [ i ] + \" \" ); } sum int sum = 0 ; for ( int i = 0 ; i < nums . length ; i ++ ) { sum += nums [ i ] ; } max (min is the same with < ) int max = nums [ 0 ] ; for ( int i = 1 ; i < nums . length ; i ++ ) { if ( nums [ i ] > max ) max = nums [ i ] ; } random shuffle for ( int i = 0 ; i < nums . length ; i ++ ) { int j = ( int ) ( math . random () * nums . length ); int temp = nums [ i ] ; nums [ i ] = nums [ j ] ; nums [ j ] = temp ; } shift left by one for ( int i = 1 ; i < nums . length ; i ++ ) { nums [ i - 1 ] = nums [ i ] ; } for-each loop for ( int value : nums ) { system . out . println ( value ); } regular for for-each uses an index yes no simpler syntax no yes can change elements yes no (assigning to value doesn't change the array) arrays model lots of things: a deck of cards ( string[] suits = {\"hearts\", \"spades\", \"clubs\", \"diamonds\"}; ), scores to analyze, players."}, {"id": "copying-arrays", "title": "Copying and passing arrays", "src": "Ch. 7", "idea": "Writing target = source does not copy an array; both names point to the same one. To copy, loop through it or use System.arraycopy or Arrays.copyOf.", "deep": "<p><strong>Copying</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">// loop</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// built in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">arraycopy</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">copy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">java</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">util</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">Arrays</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">copyOf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Passing arrays to methods</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">printArray</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">printArray</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nums</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>The method gets a copy of the reference, so changes to elements affect the caller's array (see <em>Parameters and pass-by-value</em>).</p>\n<p><strong>Variable-length arguments (varargs):</strong> the method accepts any number of values as an array.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">sum</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numbers</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numbers</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 10</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Command-line arguments:</strong> <code>args</code> in <code>main(String[] args)</code> is an array of the words typed after the class name.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>java<span class=\"w\"> </span>Test<span class=\"w\"> </span>hello<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\"># args[0] is \"hello\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Anonymous array:</strong> created without a variable, e.g. <code>printArray(new int[]{1, 2, 3});</code></li>\n</ul>", "text": "copying // loop for ( int i = 0 ; i < source . length ; i ++ ) { target [ i ] = source [ i ] ; } // built in system . arraycopy ( source , 0 , target , 0 , source . length ); int [] copy = java . util . arrays . copyof ( source , source . length ); passing arrays to methods public static void printarray ( int [] arr ) { for ( int num : arr ) { system . out . print ( num + \" \" ); } } printarray ( nums ); the method gets a copy of the reference, so changes to elements affect the caller's array (see parameters and pass-by-value ). variable-length arguments (varargs): the method accepts any number of values as an array. public static int sum ( int ... numbers ) { int total = 0 ; for ( int n : numbers ) total += n ; return total ; } sum ( 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 ); // 10 command-line arguments: args in main(string[] args) is an array of the words typed after the class name. java test hello # args[0] is \"hello\" anonymous array: created without a variable, e.g. printarray(new int[]{1, 2, 3});"}, {"id": "searching", "title": "Linear and binary search", "src": "Ch. 7", "idea": "Linear search checks every element one by one and works on any array. Binary search repeatedly halves a sorted array and is much faster, but only works if the array is sorted.", "deep": "<p><strong>Linear search: O(n)</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">linearSearch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// not found</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Binary search: O(log n), sorted arrays only</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">binarySearch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">low</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\">                     </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mid</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Linear</th>\n<th>Binary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Needs sorted array</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speed</td>\n<td>Slower</td>\n<td>Faster</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Complexity</td>\n<td>O(n)</td>\n<td>O(log n)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "linear search: o(n) public static int linearsearch ( int [] arr , int key ) { for ( int i = 0 ; i < arr . length ; i ++ ) { if ( arr [ i ] == key ) return i ; } return - 1 ; // not found } binary search: o(log n), sorted arrays only public static int binarysearch ( int [] arr , int key ) { int low = 0 ; int high = arr . length - 1 ; while ( low <= high ) { int mid = ( low + high ) / 2 ; if ( key < arr [ mid ] ) high = mid - 1 ; else if ( key > arr [ mid ] ) low = mid + 1 ; else return mid ; } return - 1 ; } linear binary needs sorted array no yes speed slower faster complexity o(n) o(log n)"}, {"id": "sorting", "title": "Selection sort and the Arrays class", "src": "Ch. 7", "idea": "Selection sort finds the smallest remaining value and swaps it into place, over and over. In real code you'd call Arrays.sort(), which does it for you.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">selectionSort</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">minIndex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">minIndex</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">minIndex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">temp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">minIndex</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">arr</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">minIndex</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">temp</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Complexity <strong>O(n²)</strong>: two nested loops over the array.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>java.util.Arrays</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.sort(nums)</code></td>\n<td>sorts in place</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.binarySearch(nums, key)</code></td>\n<td>searches a sorted array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.equals(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>same elements in the same order?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.toString(nums)</code></td>\n<td><code>\"[1, 2, 3]\"</code> for printing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.fill(nums, 0)</code></td>\n<td>sets every element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.copyOf(nums, n)</code></td>\n<td>copy with length n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Precondition:</strong> what must be true before a method runs (binary search: the array is sorted).</li>\n<li><strong>Postcondition:</strong> what's true after (selection sort: the array is sorted).</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public static void selectionsort ( int [] arr ) { for ( int i = 0 ; i < arr . length - 1 ; i ++ ) { int minindex = i ; for ( int j = i + 1 ; j < arr . length ; j ++ ) { if ( arr [ j ] < arr [ minindex ] ) minindex = j ; } int temp = arr [ i ] ; arr [ i ] = arr [ minindex ] ; arr [ minindex ] = temp ; } } complexity o(n²) : two nested loops over the array. java.util.arrays method does arrays.sort(nums) sorts in place arrays.binarysearch(nums, key) searches a sorted array arrays.equals(a, b) same elements in the same order? arrays.tostring(nums) \"[1, 2, 3]\" for printing arrays.fill(nums, 0) sets every element arrays.copyof(nums, n) copy with length n precondition: what must be true before a method runs (binary search: the array is sorted). postcondition: what's true after (selection sort: the array is sorted)."}, {"id": "arrays-2d", "title": "Two-dimensional arrays", "src": "Ch. 8, cheat sheet", "idea": "A 2D array is a table of rows and columns: really an array of arrays. You reach an element with two indexes, [row][column].", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[][]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[][]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">table</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 3 rows, 4 columns</span>\n<span class=\"n\">table</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"c1\">// row 1, column 2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Task</th>\n<th>Syntax</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Declare</td>\n<td><code>int[][] a;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create</td>\n<td><code>a = new int[rows][cols];</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Access</td>\n<td><code>a[row][col]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Number of rows</td>\n<td><code>a.length</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Columns in a row</td>\n<td><code>a[row].length</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Think of a spreadsheet, a seating chart, a game board or a matrix.</p>\n<p><strong>Ragged arrays:</strong> rows can have different lengths.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[][]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{{</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">}};</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>More dimensions:</strong> <code>int[][][] cube = new int[3][4][5];</code> is 3 layers of 4 rows × 5 columns.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> it's always <code>[row][column]</code>, and for the column count use <code>a[row].length</code>, not <code>a.length</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "int [][] matrix = { { 1 , 2 , 3 }, { 4 , 5 , 6 }, { 7 , 8 , 9 } }; int [][] table = new int [ 3 ][ 4 ] ; // 3 rows, 4 columns table [ 1 ][ 2 ] = 7 ; // row 1, column 2 task syntax declare int[][] a; create a = new int[rows][cols]; access a[row][col] number of rows a.length columns in a row a[row].length think of a spreadsheet, a seating chart, a game board or a matrix. ragged arrays: rows can have different lengths. int [][] x = {{ 1 , 2 }, { 3 , 4 , 5 }}; more dimensions: int[][][] cube = new int[3][4][5]; is 3 layers of 4 rows × 5 columns. heads up: it's always [row][column] , and for the column count use a[row].length , not a.length ."}, {"id": "arrays-2d-ops", "title": "Working with 2D arrays", "src": "Ch. 8", "idea": "Nearly every 2D array task uses nested loops: the outer loop walks the rows and the inner loop walks the columns in each row.", "deep": "<p><strong>Traverse and print</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Sum all and find the max</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrix</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">col</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Passing to a method:</strong> <code>public static void printArray(int[][] array)</code></p>\n<p><strong>Classic applications</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Grading multiple choice:</strong> <code>char[][] answers</code>, one row per student, one column per question, compared against an answer key.</li>\n<li><strong>Closest pair:</strong> <code>double[][] points</code>, each row is a point <code>{x, y}</code>. Compare every pair using the distance formula:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sudoku checker:</strong> <code>int[][] grid = new int[9][9];</code> Check that every row, every column and every 3×3 box contains 1–9.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Practice</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>new int[2][3]</code> → 2 rows, 3 columns.</li>\n<li><code>nums = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}}</code>, <code>nums[1][0]</code> → <code>3</code>.</li>\n<li><code>new int[4][5]</code> holds 20 elements.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "traverse and print for ( int row = 0 ; row < matrix . length ; row ++ ) { for ( int col = 0 ; col < matrix [ row ] . length ; col ++ ) { system . out . print ( matrix [ row ][ col ] + \" \" ); } system . out . println (); } sum all and find the max int sum = 0 ; int max = matrix [ 0 ][ 0 ] ; for ( int row = 0 ; row < matrix . length ; row ++ ) { for ( int col = 0 ; col < matrix [ row ] . length ; col ++ ) { sum += matrix [ row ][ col ] ; if ( matrix [ row ][ col ] > max ) max = matrix [ row ][ col ] ; } } passing to a method: public static void printarray(int[][] array) classic applications grading multiple choice: char[][] answers , one row per student, one column per question, compared against an answer key. closest pair: double[][] points , each row is a point {x, y} . compare every pair using the distance formula: double d = math . sqrt ( math . pow ( x2 - x1 , 2 ) + math . pow ( y2 - y1 , 2 )); sudoku checker: int[][] grid = new int[9][9]; check that every row, every column and every 3×3 box contains 1–9. practice new int[2][3] → 2 rows, 3 columns. nums = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}} , nums[1][0] → 3 . new int[4][5] holds 20 elements."}]}, {"id": "oop", "title": "Objects and classes", "blurb": "Modeling things as objects: classes, inheritance, polymorphism, abstract classes and interfaces.", "topics": [{"id": "classes-objects", "title": "Classes and objects", "src": "Ch. 9, learning plan", "idea": "A class is a blueprint, and an object is one thing built from it. The class lists the data each object holds (fields) and what it can do (methods); new creates an object.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Book</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pages</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Book</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pages</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">title</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pages</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pages</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">displayInformation</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// method</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\", \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pages</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" pages\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Book</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">book</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Book</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Dune\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">412</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// object</span>\n<span class=\"n\">book</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">displayInformation</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Class:</strong> blueprint. <strong>Object:</strong> an instance of a class.</li>\n<li>An object has <strong>state</strong> (its data), <strong>behavior</strong> (its methods) and <strong>identity</strong> (it's distinct from every other object).</li>\n<li>Parts of a class: <strong>data fields</strong> (store information), <strong>methods</strong> (actions), <strong>constructors</strong> (create objects).</li>\n<li>The <strong>dot operator</strong> reaches fields and methods: <code>student.name</code>, <code>student.study()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>UML class diagrams</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>-------------------------\n        Student\n-------------------------\n- name: String\n- age: int\n-------------------------\n+ Student()\n+ study(): void\n-------------------------\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><code>-</code> means private, <code>+</code> means public. Fields are <code>name: Type</code>, methods are <code>name(): ReturnType</code>.</p>", "text": "public class book { private string title ; private int pages ; public book ( string title , int pages ) { // constructor this . title = title ; this . pages = pages ; } public void displayinformation () { // method system . out . println ( title + \", \" + pages + \" pages\" ); } } book book = new book ( \"dune\" , 412 ); // object book . displayinformation (); class: blueprint. object: an instance of a class. an object has state (its data), behavior (its methods) and identity (it's distinct from every other object). parts of a class: data fields (store information), methods (actions), constructors (create objects). the dot operator reaches fields and methods: student.name , student.study() . uml class diagrams ------------------------- student ------------------------- - name: string - age: int ------------------------- + student() + study(): void ------------------------- - means private, + means public. fields are name: type , methods are name(): returntype ."}, {"id": "constructors", "title": "Constructors and this", "src": "Ch. 9", "idea": "A constructor sets up a new object. It has the same name as the class and no return type. Inside, this means \"the object being built\", which helps when a parameter has the same name as a field.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"c1\">// no-arg constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">                      </span><span class=\"c1\">// calls the other constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// constructor with a parameter</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"c1\">// field = parameter</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// radius 1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// radius 5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Same name as the class, <strong>no return type</strong> (not even <code>void</code>).</li>\n<li><code>this.radius</code> is the field; plain <code>radius</code> is the parameter.</li>\n<li><strong>Constructor chaining:</strong> <code>this(...)</code> calls another constructor in the same class. It must be the first line.</li>\n<li>If you write no constructor, Java gives you a default no-arg one. Once you write any constructor, that default disappears.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public class circle { private double radius ; public circle () { // no-arg constructor this ( 1 ); // calls the other constructor } public circle ( double radius ) { // constructor with a parameter this . radius = radius ; // field = parameter } } circle c1 = new circle (); // radius 1 circle c2 = new circle ( 5 ); // radius 5 same name as the class, no return type (not even void ). this.radius is the field; plain radius is the parameter. constructor chaining: this(...) calls another constructor in the same class. it must be the first line. if you write no constructor, java gives you a default no-arg one. once you write any constructor, that default disappears."}, {"id": "references", "title": "References, null and default values", "src": "Ch. 9", "idea": "A primitive variable holds its value. An object variable holds a reference (an address) to the object, so two variables can point at the same object, and a variable can point at nothing (null).", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"c1\">// holds 5</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// holds a reference</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"c1\">// both point to the SAME object</span>\n<span class=\"n\">c2</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setRadius</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">9</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// c1 sees the change too</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Default values for fields</strong> (local variables get no default)</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>numbers</td>\n<td><code>0</code> / <code>0.0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td><code>false</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td><code>'\\u0000'</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>references</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Common mistakes</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// compile error: never created</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// NullPointerException at runtime</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Arrays of objects</strong> start full of <code>null</code>, so create each object:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">circles</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// [null, null, null]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">circles</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "int x = 5 ; // holds 5 circle c1 = new circle (); // holds a reference circle c2 = c1 ; // both point to the same object c2 . setradius ( 9 ); // c1 sees the change too default values for fields (local variables get no default) type default numbers 0 / 0.0 boolean false char '\\u0000' references null common mistakes circle c ; c . radius = 5 ; // compile error: never created circle d = null ; d . radius = 5 ; // nullpointerexception at runtime arrays of objects start full of null , so create each object: circle [] circles = new circle [ 3 ] ; // [null, null, null] circles [ 0 ] = new circle ();"}, {"id": "static-instance", "title": "Static vs instance", "src": "Ch. 9", "idea": "Instance fields and methods belong to each object separately. Static ones belong to the class and are shared by every object, so you can use them without creating an object.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"c1\">// instance: each student has one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">studentCount</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// static: one shared counter</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">studentCount</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getStudentCount</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">studentCount</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getStudentCount</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// call static members on the class</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Instance</th>\n<th>Static</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>belongs to an object</td>\n<td>belongs to the class</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>needs an object</td>\n<td>no object needed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>one per object</td>\n<td>shared by all</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>A static method can't use instance fields directly (there's no \"current object\").</li>\n<li><code>public static final</code> makes a class-wide constant: <code>public static final int BALL_RADIUS = 5;</code></li>\n</ul>", "text": "public class student { private string name ; // instance: each student has one private static int studentcount = 0 ; // static: one shared counter public student ( string name ) { this . name = name ; studentcount ++ ; } public static int getstudentcount () { return studentcount ; } } student . getstudentcount (); // call static members on the class instance static belongs to an object belongs to the class needs an object no object needed one per object shared by all a static method can't use instance fields directly (there's no \"current object\"). public static final makes a class-wide constant: public static final int ball_radius = 5;"}, {"id": "encapsulation", "title": "Encapsulation, getters and setters", "src": "Ch. 9, learning plan", "idea": "Make fields private so other classes can't change them directly, then offer public getter and setter methods. Setters can check values before accepting them.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">BankAccount</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">balance</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getBalance</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// getter (accessor)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">balance</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">setBalance</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">amount</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// setter (mutator)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">amount</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"c1\">// reject bad values</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">balance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">amount</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Benefits: protects data, easier maintenance, more control.</li>\n<li>Boolean getters start with <code>is</code>: <code>public boolean isEmpty()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Immutable classes:</strong> objects that can't change after creation (like <code>String</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Person</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Person</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Rules: private fields, no setters, no methods that change fields (and don't return references to mutable fields).</p>", "text": "public class bankaccount { private double balance ; public double getbalance () { // getter (accessor) return balance ; } public void setbalance ( double amount ) { // setter (mutator) if ( amount >= 0 ) { // reject bad values balance = amount ; } } } benefits: protects data, easier maintenance, more control. boolean getters start with is : public boolean isempty() . immutable classes: objects that can't change after creation (like string ). public final class person { private final string name ; public person ( string name ) { this . name = name ; } public string getname () { return name ; } } rules: private fields, no setters, no methods that change fields (and don't return references to mutable fields)."}, {"id": "library-classes", "title": "Useful library classes", "src": "Ch. 9, Ch. 13", "idea": "Java's library has ready-made classes you create and use like your own: Random for random numbers, Point2D for coordinates, and date classes for dates and times.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Random</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Random</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rand</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 0–9</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Point2D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Point2D</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">Double</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Point2D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Point2D</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">Double</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">distance</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 5.0</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Date</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">date</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Date</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// current date and time</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Calendar and GregorianCalendar</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">GregorianCalendar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GregorianCalendar</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Calendar</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">YEAR</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Calendar</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">MONTH</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// months start at 0!</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Calendar</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">DAY_OF_MONTH</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">cal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">set</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2026</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"c1\">// May 10, 2026</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> <code>Date</code> and <code>Calendar</code> are older APIs your textbook covers. Modern code uses <code>java.time</code>: <code>LocalDate.now()</code>, <code>LocalDate.of(2026, 5, 10)</code> (months start at 1 there). <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "random rand = new random (); int n = rand . nextint ( 10 ); // 0–9 point2d p1 = new point2d . double ( 1 , 2 ); point2d p2 = new point2d . double ( 4 , 6 ); system . out . println ( p1 . distance ( p2 )); // 5.0 date date = new date (); // current date and time calendar and gregoriancalendar gregoriancalendar cal = new gregoriancalendar (); cal . get ( calendar . year ); cal . get ( calendar . month ); // months start at 0! cal . get ( calendar . day_of_month ); cal . set ( 2026 , 4 , 10 ); // may 10, 2026 tip: date and calendar are older apis your textbook covers. modern code uses java.time : localdate.now() , localdate.of(2026, 5, 10) (months start at 1 there). added by fern"}, {"id": "oop-thinking", "title": "Thinking in objects", "src": "Ch. 10, Ch. 13", "idea": "Object-oriented design asks \"which object does this?\" instead of \"which steps happen?\". You find the objects, give them fields and methods, then decide how they relate.", "deep": "<p><strong>Class abstraction:</strong> users of a class care about <em>what</em> it does (its public methods), not <em>how</em>. The inside can change without breaking code that uses it. The public methods and their promises are the <strong>class contract</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Procedural</th>\n<th>Object-oriented</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>focuses on functions</td>\n<td>focuses on objects</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>data and behavior separate</td>\n<td>data and methods bundled together</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\"What actions happen?\"</td>\n<td>\"Which object does the action?\"</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Relationships between classes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Has-a:</strong> one class holds another as a field (<code>Car</code> has an <code>Engine</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Aggregation:</strong> weak has-a; the parts can exist on their own (a team and its players).</li>\n<li><strong>Composition:</strong> strong has-a; the part can't exist without the whole (a house and its rooms).</li>\n<li><strong>Multiplicity:</strong> how many objects take part (one-to-one, one-to-many).</li>\n<li><strong>Is-a:</strong> inheritance (see <em>Inheritance and super</em>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Design steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Identify the objects.</li>\n<li>Define their fields.</li>\n<li>Define their methods.</li>\n<li>Set up relationships.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Class design guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Encapsulation:</strong> private fields, public methods.</li>\n<li><strong>Cohesion:</strong> one class, one clear purpose.</li>\n<li><strong>Clear naming:</strong> <code>BankAccount</code>, not <code>DataStuff</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Minimize side effects:</strong> methods shouldn't change data unexpectedly.</li>\n<li><strong>Reusability:</strong> design classes you could use in other programs.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "class abstraction: users of a class care about what it does (its public methods), not how . the inside can change without breaking code that uses it. the public methods and their promises are the class contract . procedural object-oriented focuses on functions focuses on objects data and behavior separate data and methods bundled together \"what actions happen?\" \"which object does the action?\" relationships between classes has-a: one class holds another as a field ( car has an engine ). aggregation: weak has-a; the parts can exist on their own (a team and its players). composition: strong has-a; the part can't exist without the whole (a house and its rooms). multiplicity: how many objects take part (one-to-one, one-to-many). is-a: inheritance (see inheritance and super ). design steps identify the objects. define their fields. define their methods. set up relationships. class design guidelines encapsulation: private fields, public methods. cohesion: one class, one clear purpose. clear naming: bankaccount , not datastuff . minimize side effects: methods shouldn't change data unexpectedly. reusability: design classes you could use in other programs."}, {"id": "wrappers", "title": "Wrapper classes, BigInteger and BigDecimal", "src": "Ch. 10, Ch. 13", "idea": "Wrapper classes (Integer, Double…) let primitives act as objects, which collections need. BigInteger and BigDecimal handle numbers too big or too precise for primitives.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Primitive</th>\n<th>Wrapper</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>int</code></td>\n<td><code>Integer</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>double</code></td>\n<td><code>Double</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td><code>Character</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td><code>Boolean</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Boxing and unboxing</strong> happen automatically:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">obj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// boxing: int → Integer</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">obj</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"c1\">// unboxing: Integer → int</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>Number</code> is the abstract superclass of <code>Integer</code>, <code>Double</code>, <code>Long</code>, <code>BigInteger</code>, <code>BigDecimal</code> and others.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>BigInteger and BigDecimal</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">BigInteger</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigInteger</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"12345678901234567890\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">BigInteger</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigInteger</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// no + operator!</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">BigDecimal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">price</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigDecimal</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"19.99\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">BigDecimal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">price</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">multiply</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigDecimal</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"3\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Use methods: <code>add</code>, <code>subtract</code>, <code>multiply</code>, <code>divide</code>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>BigDecimal</code> (built from a String) for money, since <code>double</code> can't store 0.1 exactly.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "primitive wrapper int integer double double char character boolean boolean boxing and unboxing happen automatically: integer obj = 5 ; // boxing: int → integer int x = obj ; // unboxing: integer → int number is the abstract superclass of integer , double , long , biginteger , bigdecimal and others. biginteger and bigdecimal biginteger a = new biginteger ( \"12345678901234567890\" ); biginteger b = a . add ( new biginteger ( \"1\" )); // no + operator! bigdecimal price = new bigdecimal ( \"19.99\" ); bigdecimal total = price . multiply ( new bigdecimal ( \"3\" )); use methods: add , subtract , multiply , divide . use bigdecimal (built from a string) for money, since double can't store 0.1 exactly."}, {"id": "inheritance", "title": "Inheritance and super", "src": "Ch. 11, learning plan", "idea": "A subclass extends a superclass and inherits its fields and methods, then adds or changes what it needs. Only use it when the subclass truly \"is a\" kind of the superclass.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Employee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Employee</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">calculatePay</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hourlyRate</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hoursWorked</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rate</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hours</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\">// runs Employee's constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hourlyRate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rate</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hoursWorked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hours</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">calculatePay</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hourlyRate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hoursWorked</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>superclass (parent)</td>\n<td>the class being inherited from</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>subclass (child)</td>\n<td>the class that inherits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>supertype / subtype</td>\n<td>the types those classes define</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Is-a test:</strong> Dog is-a Animal, Circle is-a Shape, Student is-a Person. If it doesn't read naturally, don't use inheritance.</li>\n<li>Java allows <strong>single inheritance</strong>: a class extends exactly one class.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Using <code>super</code></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>super(name)</code> calls the superclass constructor. It must be the <strong>first line</strong> of the constructor.</li>\n<li><code>super.sound()</code> calls the superclass's version of a method.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Dog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Animal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">sound</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sound</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"Animal sound\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Dog bark\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Constructor chaining:</strong> creating a <code>Student</code> runs <code>Student()</code> → <code>super()</code> → <code>Person()</code> → <code>Object()</code>. If you don't write <code>super(...)</code>, Java inserts <code>super()</code> for you, so the superclass needs a no-arg constructor.</p>", "text": "public class employee { private string name ; public employee ( string name ) { this . name = name ; } public string getname () { return name ; } public double calculatepay () { return 0.0 ; } } public class hourlyemployee extends employee { private double hourlyrate ; private double hoursworked ; public hourlyemployee ( string name , double rate , double hours ) { super ( name ); // runs employee's constructor this . hourlyrate = rate ; this . hoursworked = hours ; } @override public double calculatepay () { return hourlyrate * hoursworked ; } } term meaning superclass (parent) the class being inherited from subclass (child) the class that inherits supertype / subtype the types those classes define is-a test: dog is-a animal, circle is-a shape, student is-a person. if it doesn't read naturally, don't use inheritance. java allows single inheritance : a class extends exactly one class. using super super(name) calls the superclass constructor. it must be the first line of the constructor. super.sound() calls the superclass's version of a method. class dog extends animal { @override void sound () { super . sound (); // \"animal sound\" system . out . println ( \"dog bark\" ); } } constructor chaining: creating a student runs student() → super() → person() → object() . if you don't write super(...) , java inserts super() for you, so the superclass needs a no-arg constructor."}, {"id": "overriding", "title": "Overriding, the Object class and toString", "src": "Ch. 11", "idea": "Overriding means a subclass replaces an inherited method with its own version, using the exact same signature. Every class ultimately extends Object, so every class can override toString() and equals().", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Animal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">sound</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Animal sound\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Dog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Animal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">sound</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Bark\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Overriding rules:</strong> same name, same parameters, same (or compatible) return type, and access can't be more restrictive.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@Override</code> asks the compiler to check that you really are overriding. A typo then becomes a compile error instead of a silent new method.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Overriding</th>\n<th>Overloading</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>in a subclass</td>\n<td>in the same class (or a subclass)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>same signature</td>\n<td>different parameters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>chosen at runtime</td>\n<td>chosen at compile time</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>The Object class:</strong> every class inherits from <code>java.lang.Object</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>toString()</code></td>\n<td>text description of the object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>equals(Object o)</code></td>\n<td>are two objects equal?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hashCode()</code></td>\n<td>hash value (override it whenever you override equals)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>getClass()</code></td>\n<td>runtime class information</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Person</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">toString</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Person: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// calls toString() automatically</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "class animal { void sound () { system . out . println ( \"animal sound\" ); } } class dog extends animal { @override void sound () { system . out . println ( \"bark\" ); } } overriding rules: same name, same parameters, same (or compatible) return type, and access can't be more restrictive. @override asks the compiler to check that you really are overriding. a typo then becomes a compile error instead of a silent new method. overriding overloading in a subclass in the same class (or a subclass) same signature different parameters chosen at runtime chosen at compile time the object class: every class inherits from java.lang.object . method purpose tostring() text description of the object equals(object o) are two objects equal? hashcode() hash value (override it whenever you override equals) getclass() runtime class information class person { private string name ; @override public string tostring () { return \"person: \" + name ; } } system . out . println ( p ); // calls tostring() automatically"}, {"id": "polymorphism", "title": "Polymorphism", "src": "learning plan, cheat sheet", "idea": "A superclass variable can hold any subclass object. When you call an overridden method, Java runs the version for the actual object, not the variable's type. That's polymorphism.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Jordan\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">20.00</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">35</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">calculatePay</span><span class=\"p\">());</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// runs HourlyEmployee's version: 700.0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Two types, two jobs</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>declared type</strong> (left side, <code>Employee</code>) decides what the <strong>compiler</strong> lets you call.</li>\n<li>The <strong>actual type</strong> (right side, <code>HourlyEmployee</code>) decides which overridden version <strong>runs</strong>. This is called <strong>dynamic binding</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"p\">(...);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// OK: an HourlyEmployee is an Employee</span>\n<span class=\"n\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"p\">(...);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// error: not every Employee is hourly</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Why it's useful:</strong> one loop can handle many kinds of objects.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">staff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">staff</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Jordan\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">35</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">staff</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SalariedEmployee</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Sam\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">52000</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Employee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">emp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">staff</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">emp</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\": \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">emp</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">calculatePay</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> your learning plan flags overriding as a tricky spot. The fastest way to see it: make a parent-type variable, put different child objects in it, and call the same method. Watch the output change. <span class=\"by\">From your learning plan</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Casting objects:</strong> to call a subclass-only method, check and cast:</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">instanceof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HourlyEmployee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// Java 16+ pattern matching</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// use h here</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "employee e = new hourlyemployee ( \"jordan\" , 20.00 , 35 ); system . out . println ( e . calculatepay ()); // runs hourlyemployee's version: 700.0 two types, two jobs the declared type (left side, employee ) decides what the compiler lets you call. the actual type (right side, hourlyemployee ) decides which overridden version runs . this is called dynamic binding . employee a = new hourlyemployee (...); // ok: an hourlyemployee is an employee hourlyemployee b = new employee (...); // error: not every employee is hourly why it's useful: one loop can handle many kinds of objects. arraylist < employee > staff = new arraylist <> (); staff . add ( new hourlyemployee ( \"jordan\" , 20 , 35 )); staff . add ( new salariedemployee ( \"sam\" , 52000 )); for ( employee emp : staff ) { system . out . println ( emp . getname () + \": \" + emp . calculatepay ()); } tip: your learning plan flags overriding as a tricky spot. the fastest way to see it: make a parent-type variable, put different child objects in it, and call the same method. watch the output change. from your learning plan casting objects: to call a subclass-only method, check and cast: if ( e instanceof hourlyemployee h ) { // java 16+ pattern matching // use h here }"}, {"id": "abstract-classes", "title": "Abstract classes", "src": "Ch. 13, learning plan", "idea": "An abstract class is a general template you can't create objects from. It can declare abstract methods (no body) that every concrete subclass must fill in.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">abstract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">abstract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getArea</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// no body</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getArea</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">PI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>new Shape()</code> is a compile error. <code>Shape s = new Circle(2);</code> is fine.</li>\n<li>A class with any abstract method must itself be abstract.</li>\n<li>A subclass must implement <strong>all</strong> inherited abstract methods, or be abstract too.</li>\n<li>Abstract classes can still have fields, constructors and normal methods.</li>\n<li>Use one when related classes share behavior, but some methods only make sense in the subclasses. <code>Shape</code> says <strong>what</strong> every shape does, not <strong>how</strong>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public abstract class shape { public abstract double getarea (); // no body } public class circle extends shape { private double radius ; public circle ( double radius ) { this . radius = radius ; } @override public double getarea () { return math . pi * radius * radius ; } } new shape() is a compile error. shape s = new circle(2); is fine. a class with any abstract method must itself be abstract. a subclass must implement all inherited abstract methods, or be abstract too. abstract classes can still have fields, constructors and normal methods. use one when related classes share behavior, but some methods only make sense in the subclasses. shape says what every shape does, not how ."}, {"id": "interfaces", "title": "Interfaces", "src": "Ch. 13, learning plan", "idea": "An interface lists behaviors a class promises to provide. A class can implement many interfaces, which lets unrelated classes (a Bird and an Airplane) share a capability like Flyable.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">interface</span> <span class=\"nc\">Flyable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">fly</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// implicitly public and abstract</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Bird</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Flyable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">fly</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Bird is flying\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Robot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Flyable</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Movable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// several interfaces</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Interfaces can contain constants, abstract methods, <code>default</code> methods (with a body) and <code>static</code> methods.</li>\n<li>They <strong>can't</strong> have instance fields or constructors.</li>\n<li>An interface can extend another (<strong>subinterface</strong>): <code>interface B extends A {}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Marker interface:</strong> an empty interface that just tags a capability (<code>Cloneable</code>, <code>Serializable</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Functional interface:</strong> exactly one abstract method, so it can be written as a lambda (see <em>JavaFX → Handlers and lambdas</em>).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Concrete class</th>\n<th>Abstract class</th>\n<th>Interface</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Create objects?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Constructors?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fields?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Constants only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Abstract methods?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Inherit several?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "public interface flyable { void fly (); // implicitly public and abstract } public class bird implements flyable { @override public void fly () { system . out . println ( \"bird is flying\" ); } } class robot implements flyable , movable { } // several interfaces interfaces can contain constants, abstract methods, default methods (with a body) and static methods. they can't have instance fields or constructors. an interface can extend another ( subinterface ): interface b extends a {} . marker interface: an empty interface that just tags a capability ( cloneable , serializable ). functional interface: exactly one abstract method, so it can be written as a lambda (see javafx → handlers and lambdas ). concrete class abstract class interface create objects? yes no no constructors? yes yes no fields? yes yes constants only abstract methods? no yes yes inherit several? no no yes"}, {"id": "comparable", "title": "Comparable and Comparator", "src": "Ch. 13, Ch. 20, learning plan", "idea": "Comparable gives a class one natural order (its compareTo method), which Arrays.sort and Collections.sort use. A Comparator is a separate rule you pass in when you want a different order.", "deep": "<p><strong>Comparable: the class sorts itself</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Comparable</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gpa</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">compareTo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">other</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Double</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">compare</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">gpa</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">other</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">gpa</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Collections</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sort</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">studentList</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// uses compareTo</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code>compareTo</code> returns</th>\n<th>Means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>negative</td>\n<td>this comes before other</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>positive</td>\n<td>this comes after other</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Used by <code>Arrays.sort()</code>, <code>Collections.sort()</code>, <code>TreeSet</code>, <code>TreeMap</code>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> your notes use <code>return this.id - s.id;</code>. It works for small numbers but can overflow with large ones. <code>Integer.compare(this.id, s.id)</code> is the safe version. <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Comparator: an outside sorting rule</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Comparator</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">byName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">compareTo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s2</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Collections</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sort</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">byName</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">sort</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Comparator</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">comparing</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">getName</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// same thing, shorter</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Use a Comparator when the class doesn't implement Comparable, or when you need more than one sort order.</p>", "text": "comparable: the class sorts itself public class student implements comparable < student > { private string name ; private double gpa ; @override public int compareto ( student other ) { return double . compare ( this . gpa , other . gpa ); } } collections . sort ( studentlist ); // uses compareto compareto returns means negative this comes before other 0 equal positive this comes after other used by arrays.sort() , collections.sort() , treeset , treemap . tip: your notes use return this.id - s.id; . it works for small numbers but can overflow with large ones. integer.compare(this.id, s.id) is the safe version. added by fern comparator: an outside sorting rule comparator < student > byname = ( s1 , s2 ) -> s1 . getname (). compareto ( s2 . getname ()); collections . sort ( list , byname ); list . sort ( comparator . comparing ( student :: getname )); // same thing, shorter use a comparator when the class doesn't implement comparable, or when you need more than one sort order."}, {"id": "cloning", "title": "Cloning: shallow vs deep copy", "src": "Ch. 13", "idea": "Implementing Cloneable lets an object be copied with clone(). A shallow copy shares the objects inside it with the original; a deep copy duplicates those too, so the two are fully independent.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Person</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Cloneable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Person</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">clone</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">throws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CloneNotSupportedException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Person</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">clone</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Person</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">clone</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>Cloneable</code> is a <strong>marker interface</strong>: no methods, it just allows cloning.</li>\n<li><strong>Shallow copy:</strong> copies field values. Reference fields still point to the same inner objects, so changing one affects both.</li>\n<li><strong>Deep copy:</strong> also copies the inner objects. Fully independent.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> <code>Person copy = original;</code> (in the notes' shallow-copy example) isn't a copy at all. It's a second reference to the same object. A shallow copy is a new outer object that shares the inner ones. <span class=\"by\">Clarified by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "class person implements cloneable { @override public person clone () throws clonenotsupportedexception { return ( person ) super . clone (); } } person p2 = p1 . clone (); cloneable is a marker interface : no methods, it just allows cloning. shallow copy: copies field values. reference fields still point to the same inner objects, so changing one affects both. deep copy: also copies the inner objects. fully independent. heads up: person copy = original; (in the notes' shallow-copy example) isn't a copy at all. it's a second reference to the same object. a shallow copy is a new outer object that shares the inner ones. clarified by fern"}, {"id": "records", "title": "Records", "src": "Ch. 13", "idea": "A record is a one-line way to write a simple, immutable data class. Java generates the constructor, getters, toString, equals and hashCode for you.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">record</span> <span class=\"nc\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Noah\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"p\">());</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// getters use the field name, no \"get\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// Student[name=Noah, age=20]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Fields are final, so records are immutable.</li>\n<li>Good for simple data carriers. Cuts out boilerplate.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "record student ( string name , int age ) {} student s = new student ( \"noah\" , 20 ); system . out . println ( s . name ()); // getters use the field name, no \"get\" system . out . println ( s ); // student[name=noah, age=20] fields are final, so records are immutable. good for simple data carriers. cuts out boilerplate."}, {"id": "rational-example", "title": "Example: a Rational class", "src": "Ch. 13", "idea": "The Rational class is a worked example of good class design: a fraction type that extends Number, implements Comparable, and keeps itself simplified.", "deep": "<ul>\n<li>A rational number is a fraction: 1/2, 3/4, 5/8.</li>\n<li>Typical methods: <code>add</code>, <code>subtract</code>, <code>multiply</code>, <code>divide</code>, plus simplifying with the greatest common divisor.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Rational</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rational</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Rational</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rational</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 5/4</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>It practices immutability (each operation returns a new Rational), <code>toString</code>, <code>equals</code>, and <code>compareTo</code>.</p>", "text": "a rational number is a fraction: 1/2, 3/4, 5/8. typical methods: add , subtract , multiply , divide , plus simplifying with the greatest common divisor. rational r1 = new rational ( 1 , 2 ); rational r2 = new rational ( 3 , 4 ); system . out . println ( r1 . add ( r2 )); // 5/4 it practices immutability (each operation returns a new rational), tostring , equals , and compareto ."}]}, {"id": "exceptions-io", "title": "Exceptions and file I/O", "blurb": "Handling errors gracefully, and reading and writing files.", "topics": [{"id": "exception-basics", "title": "What exceptions are", "src": "Ch. 12", "idea": "An exception is an object Java creates when something goes wrong while running. Checked exceptions must be handled or declared, or the code won't compile; unchecked ones (RuntimeException) don't have to be.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>Throwable\n ├── Error              (serious, don't catch: OutOfMemoryError)\n └── Exception          (recoverable: IOException)\n      └── RuntimeException   (programming bugs: NullPointerException)\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Checked by compiler?</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Checked</td>\n<td>Yes: handle or declare it</td>\n<td><code>IOException</code>, <code>FileNotFoundException</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unchecked</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td><code>NullPointerException</code>, <code>ArithmeticException</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>RuntimeException</code>, <code>Error</code> and their subclasses are <strong>unchecked</strong>. Everything else is <strong>checked</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common exceptions</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Exception</th>\n<th>Cause</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ArithmeticException</code></td>\n<td>integer divide by zero</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NullPointerException</code></td>\n<td>using a null reference</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException</code></td>\n<td>bad array index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>InputMismatchException</code></td>\n<td>Scanner got the wrong type</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NumberFormatException</code></td>\n<td><code>Integer.parseInt(\"abc\")</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FileNotFoundException</code></td>\n<td>file missing</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Why use exception handling:</strong> separates error handling from normal code, prevents crashes, and lets the program recover.</p>", "text": "throwable ├── error (serious, don't catch: outofmemoryerror) └── exception (recoverable: ioexception) └── runtimeexception (programming bugs: nullpointerexception) type checked by compiler? example checked yes: handle or declare it ioexception , filenotfoundexception unchecked no nullpointerexception , arithmeticexception runtimeexception , error and their subclasses are unchecked . everything else is checked . common exceptions exception cause arithmeticexception integer divide by zero nullpointerexception using a null reference arrayindexoutofboundsexception bad array index inputmismatchexception scanner got the wrong type numberformatexception integer.parseint(\"abc\") filenotfoundexception file missing why use exception handling: separates error handling from normal code, prevents crashes, and lets the program recover."}, {"id": "try-catch", "title": "try, catch and finally", "src": "Ch. 12", "idea": "Put risky code in try. If an exception happens, Java jumps to the matching catch block, then carries on. finally always runs, error or not, which makes it the place for cleanup.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ArithmeticException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Cannot divide by zero\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">finally</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Always runs\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Flow:</strong> the try block runs → an exception occurs → the rest of try is skipped → the matching catch runs → finally runs → the program continues.</p>\n<p><strong>Several catch blocks:</strong> list the most specific first.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// ...</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileNotFoundException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// subclass first</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// ...</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IOException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"c1\">// superclass after</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// ...</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Putting the superclass first is a compile error, because the subclass block could never be reached.</p>\n<p><strong>Useful exception methods</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>getMessage()</code></td>\n<td>the error message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>toString()</code></td>\n<td>exception class + message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>printStackTrace()</code></td>\n<td>prints the full trace of method calls</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "try { int x = 5 / 0 ; } catch ( arithmeticexception ex ) { system . out . println ( \"cannot divide by zero\" ); } finally { system . out . println ( \"always runs\" ); } flow: the try block runs → an exception occurs → the rest of try is skipped → the matching catch runs → finally runs → the program continues. several catch blocks: list the most specific first. try { // ... } catch ( filenotfoundexception ex ) { // subclass first // ... } catch ( ioexception ex ) { // superclass after // ... } putting the superclass first is a compile error, because the subclass block could never be reached. useful exception methods method returns getmessage() the error message tostring() exception class + message printstacktrace() prints the full trace of method calls"}, {"id": "throw-throws", "title": "throw, throws and custom exceptions", "src": "Ch. 12", "idea": "throw creates an exception right now. throws in a method header warns callers that the method might throw one. If nobody catches it, the exception travels up the call chain until something does, or the program ends.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Keyword</th>\n<th>Where</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>throw</code></td>\n<td>in the body</td>\n<td>actually throws an exception</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>throws</code></td>\n<td>in the header</td>\n<td>declares the method may throw it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">setAge</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IllegalArgumentException</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Age cannot be negative\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">readFile</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">throws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IOException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Propagation:</strong> an uncaught exception passes from <code>method3 → method2 → method1 → main</code>. If it's never caught, the program stops and prints the stack trace.</p>\n<p><strong>Rethrowing:</strong> catch it, do something (like logging), then pass it on with <code>throw ex;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Chained exceptions:</strong> wrap the original cause so it isn't lost: <code>new Exception(\"Load failed\", originalException)</code> or <code>ex.initCause(original)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Custom exceptions</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">InvalidAgeException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">InvalidAgeException</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InvalidAgeException</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Age cannot be negative\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>When not to use exceptions:</strong> for ordinary checks, a plain <code>if</code> is clearer and faster. Save exceptions for unexpected problems.</p>", "text": "keyword where purpose throw in the body actually throws an exception throws in the header declares the method may throw it public void setage ( int age ) { if ( age < 0 ) { throw new illegalargumentexception ( \"age cannot be negative\" ); } this . age = age ; } public void readfile () throws ioexception { ... } propagation: an uncaught exception passes from method3 → method2 → method1 → main . if it's never caught, the program stops and prints the stack trace. rethrowing: catch it, do something (like logging), then pass it on with throw ex; . chained exceptions: wrap the original cause so it isn't lost: new exception(\"load failed\", originalexception) or ex.initcause(original) . custom exceptions public class invalidageexception extends exception { public invalidageexception ( string message ) { super ( message ); } } throw new invalidageexception ( \"age cannot be negative\" ); when not to use exceptions: for ordinary checks, a plain if is clearer and faster. save exceptions for unexpected problems."}, {"id": "files-paths", "title": "The File class and paths", "src": "Ch. 12", "idea": "A File object represents a file or folder path. It can check whether the file exists, rename or delete it, and make folders, but it doesn't read or write contents.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">File</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">File</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"data.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">exists</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" bytes\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>exists()</code></td>\n<td>does it exist?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>length()</code></td>\n<td>size in bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>delete()</code></td>\n<td>deletes it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>renameTo(File)</code></td>\n<td>renames it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>mkdir()</code></td>\n<td>creates a folder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>isDirectory()</code> / <code>isFile()</code></td>\n<td>which kind is it?</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Path type</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n<th>Starts from</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Absolute</td>\n<td><code>/Users/noah/data.txt</code> or <code>C:\\Users\\Noah\\data.txt</code></td>\n<td>the root</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Relative</td>\n<td><code>data.txt</code></td>\n<td>the current project folder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "file file = new file ( \"data.txt\" ); if ( file . exists ()) { system . out . println ( file . length () + \" bytes\" ); } method does exists() does it exist? length() size in bytes delete() deletes it renameto(file) renames it mkdir() creates a folder isdirectory() / isfile() which kind is it? path type example starts from absolute /users/noah/data.txt or c:\\users\\noah\\data.txt the root relative data.txt the current project folder"}, {"id": "text-files", "title": "Reading and writing text files", "src": "Ch. 12, learning plan", "idea": "Write text with PrintWriter and read it with Scanner. Wrap them in try-with-resources so the file closes automatically, even if something goes wrong.", "deep": "<p><strong>Write</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PrintWriter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrintWriter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"tasks.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Study collections\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Practice exceptions\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileNotFoundException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"The file could not be created.\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Read</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileInput</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">File</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"tasks.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fileInput</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hasNextLine</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fileInput</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextLine</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileNotFoundException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"The file was not found.\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>try-with-resources:</strong> anything declared in <code>try ( ... )</code> is closed automatically. No <code>close()</code> needed.</li>\n<li>Without it, always call <code>close()</code>, ideally in <code>finally</code>, or written data may never reach the file.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Replacing text in a file:</strong> read the original with Scanner, change each line with <code>String.replace()</code>, write the result to a new file with PrintWriter.</p>", "text": "write try ( printwriter output = new printwriter ( \"tasks.txt\" )) { output . println ( \"study collections\" ); output . println ( \"practice exceptions\" ); } catch ( filenotfoundexception ex ) { system . out . println ( \"the file could not be created.\" ); } read try ( scanner fileinput = new scanner ( new file ( \"tasks.txt\" ))) { while ( fileinput . hasnextline ()) { system . out . println ( fileinput . nextline ()); } } catch ( filenotfoundexception ex ) { system . out . println ( \"the file was not found.\" ); } try-with-resources: anything declared in try ( ... ) is closed automatically. no close() needed. without it, always call close() , ideally in finally , or written data may never reach the file. replacing text in a file: read the original with scanner, change each line with string.replace() , write the result to a new file with printwriter."}, {"id": "web-data", "title": "Reading data from the web", "src": "Ch. 12", "idea": "Java can read a web page like a file: open a URL's stream and hand it to a Scanner. A web crawler repeats this, following the links it finds.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">URL</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">url</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">URI</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">create</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"https://example.com\"</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"na\">toURL</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">url</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">openStream</span><span class=\"p\">()))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hasNextLine</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextLine</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> your notes use <code>new URL(\"https://...\")</code>. That constructor is deprecated since Java 20; on Java 21 use <code>URI.create(...).toURL()</code> as above. <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Web crawler steps</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Start from one URL.</li>\n<li>Read the page text.</li>\n<li>Extract the links.</li>\n<li>Visit each new link and repeat (keeping a list of pages already visited).</li>\n</ol>", "text": "url url = uri . create ( \"https://example.com\" ). tourl (); try ( scanner input = new scanner ( url . openstream ())) { while ( input . hasnextline ()) { system . out . println ( input . nextline ()); } } heads up: your notes use new url(\"https://...\") . that constructor is deprecated since java 20; on java 21 use uri.create(...).tourl() as above. added by fern web crawler steps start from one url. read the page text. extract the links. visit each new link and repeat (keeping a list of pages already visited)."}, {"id": "streams", "title": "Streams: text vs binary I/O", "src": "Ch. 17", "idea": "All Java I/O flows through streams. Input streams bring data into the program and output streams send it out. Text I/O stores readable characters; binary I/O stores raw bytes.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Direction</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>InputStream</code></td>\n<td>data flows <strong>into</strong> the program</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OutputStream</code></td>\n<td>data flows <strong>out of</strong> the program</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Text I/O</th>\n<th>Binary I/O</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Human-readable</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stores raw bytes</td>\n<td>No (uses an encoding like UTF-8)</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speed / size</td>\n<td>Slower, larger</td>\n<td>Faster, smaller</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Best for</td>\n<td>.txt, .csv, logs, config files</td>\n<td>images, audio, video, saved objects</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>InputStream                  OutputStream\n ├── FileInputStream          ├── FileOutputStream\n ├── BufferedInputStream      ├── BufferedOutputStream\n ├── DataInputStream          ├── DataOutputStream\n └── ObjectInputStream        └── ObjectOutputStream\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "type direction inputstream data flows into the program outputstream data flows out of the program text i/o binary i/o human-readable yes no stores raw bytes no (uses an encoding like utf-8) yes speed / size slower, larger faster, smaller best for .txt, .csv, logs, config files images, audio, video, saved objects inputstream outputstream ├── fileinputstream ├── fileoutputstream ├── bufferedinputstream ├── bufferedoutputstream ├── datainputstream ├── dataoutputstream └── objectinputstream └── objectoutputstream"}, {"id": "byte-streams", "title": "Byte streams and copying files", "src": "Ch. 17", "idea": "FileInputStream reads one byte at a time and FileOutputStream writes bytes. read() returns -1 at the end of the file, which is how a copy loop knows when to stop.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"data.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">65</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// writes the byte for 'A'</span>\n<span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">close</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">append</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"data.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// true = append</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Copying a file byte by byte</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileInputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"source.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"target.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">read</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// -1 means end of file</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "fileoutputstream output = new fileoutputstream ( \"data.dat\" ); output . write ( 65 ); // writes the byte for 'a' output . close (); fileoutputstream append = new fileoutputstream ( \"data.dat\" , true ); // true = append copying a file byte by byte try ( fileinputstream input = new fileinputstream ( \"source.txt\" ); fileoutputstream output = new fileoutputstream ( \"target.txt\" )) { int data ; while (( data = input . read ()) != - 1 ) { // -1 means end of file output . write ( data ); } }"}, {"id": "data-buffered-streams", "title": "Data and buffered streams", "src": "Ch. 17", "idea": "Filter streams wrap other streams to add features. DataOutputStream writes whole ints, doubles and strings; buffered streams group bytes into chunks so there are fewer slow disk reads.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DataOutputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DataOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"numbers.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">writeInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">writeDouble</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">3.14</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">writeUTF</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DataInputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DataInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"numbers.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">readInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">readDouble</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">readUTF</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> read values back in <strong>exactly the same order</strong> you wrote them. Reading in a different order gives garbage or an error.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Buffering:</strong> without a buffer, every byte can mean a disk access. A buffer collects data into chunks first.</p>\n<p><strong>Layering streams</strong> (each wraps the next):</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">DataInputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DataInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BufferedInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"data.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)));</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "try ( dataoutputstream out = new dataoutputstream ( new fileoutputstream ( \"numbers.dat\" ))) { out . writeint ( 42 ); out . writedouble ( 3.14 ); out . writeutf ( \"hello\" ); } try ( datainputstream in = new datainputstream ( new fileinputstream ( \"numbers.dat\" ))) { int x = in . readint (); double y = in . readdouble (); string s = in . readutf (); } heads up: read values back in exactly the same order you wrote them. reading in a different order gives garbage or an error. buffering: without a buffer, every byte can mean a disk access. a buffer collects data into chunks first. layering streams (each wraps the next): datainputstream input = new datainputstream ( new bufferedinputstream ( new fileinputstream ( \"data.dat\" )));"}, {"id": "serialization", "title": "Object serialization", "src": "Ch. 17", "idea": "Serialization turns a whole object into bytes so you can save it to a file; deserialization rebuilds it. The class must implement Serializable.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Serializable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ObjectOutputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ObjectOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileOutputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"objects.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">writeObject</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">student</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ObjectInputStream</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ObjectInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FileInputStream</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"objects.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Student</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">readObject</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>Serializable</code> is a <strong>marker interface</strong>: no methods, it just says \"this can be saved\".</li>\n<li>Without it you get a <code>NotSerializableException</code>.</li>\n<li>Arrays can be serialized too: <code>out.writeObject(numbers);</code> then <code>(int[]) in.readObject()</code>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public class student implements serializable { private string name ; private int age ; } try ( objectoutputstream out = new objectoutputstream ( new fileoutputstream ( \"objects.dat\" ))) { out . writeobject ( student ); } try ( objectinputstream in = new objectinputstream ( new fileinputstream ( \"objects.dat\" ))) { student s = ( student ) in . readobject (); } serializable is a marker interface : no methods, it just says \"this can be saved\". without it you get a notserializableexception . arrays can be serialized too: out.writeobject(numbers); then (int[]) in.readobject() ."}, {"id": "random-access", "title": "Random-access files", "src": "Ch. 17", "idea": "Normal streams read a file in order, start to end. RandomAccessFile lets you jump straight to any byte position with seek() and read or write there.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">RandomAccessFile</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RandomAccessFile</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"test.dat\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"rw\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">seek</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"c1\">// jump to byte 4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">writeInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getFilePointer</span><span class=\"p\">());</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 8</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Mode</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"r\"</code></td>\n<td>read only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"rw\"</code></td>\n<td>read and write</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>seek(pos)</code></td>\n<td>move the file pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>getFilePointer()</code></td>\n<td>current position</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>length()</code></td>\n<td>file size</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>File pointer:</strong> marks the current byte position.</li>\n<li><strong>Sequential access:</strong> beginning → middle → end, in order. <strong>Random access:</strong> jump anywhere.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "try ( randomaccessfile file = new randomaccessfile ( \"test.dat\" , \"rw\" )) { file . seek ( 4 ); // jump to byte 4 file . writeint ( 100 ); system . out . println ( file . getfilepointer ()); // 8 } mode meaning \"r\" read only \"rw\" read and write method does seek(pos) move the file pointer getfilepointer() current position length() file size file pointer: marks the current byte position. sequential access: beginning → middle → end, in order. random access: jump anywhere."}]}, {"id": "collections", "title": "Collections", "blurb": "Lists, stacks, queues, sets and maps from the Java Collections Framework.", "topics": [{"id": "jcf-overview", "title": "The Collections Framework", "src": "Ch. 20", "idea": "The Java Collections Framework is a set of interfaces and classes for storing groups of objects. Collection is the root interface; List, Queue and Set build on it, and Map sits alongside for key-value pairs.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>Collection\n ├── List          ArrayList, LinkedList, Vector → Stack\n ├── Queue         LinkedList, PriorityQueue\n └── Set           HashSet, LinkedHashSet, TreeSet\n\nMap (separate)     HashMap, LinkedHashMap, TreeMap\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Methods every Collection has</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add(e)</code></td>\n<td>adds an element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remove(o)</code></td>\n<td>removes an element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>size()</code></td>\n<td>number of elements</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>isEmpty()</code></td>\n<td>true if none</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>contains(o)</code></td>\n<td>is it in there?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>clear()</code></td>\n<td>removes everything</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Collection</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Apple\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Banana\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">size</span><span class=\"p\">());</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Collections hold <strong>objects</strong>, so primitives get boxed (<code>ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;</code>, not <code>ArrayList&lt;int&gt;</code>).</li>\n<li>Most collection classes are <code>Cloneable</code> and <code>Serializable</code>, and all are <code>Iterable</code> (you can loop over them).</li>\n</ul>", "text": "collection ├── list arraylist, linkedlist, vector → stack ├── queue linkedlist, priorityqueue └── set hashset, linkedhashset, treeset map (separate) hashmap, linkedhashmap, treemap methods every collection has method does add(e) adds an element remove(o) removes an element size() number of elements isempty() true if none contains(o) is it in there? clear() removes everything collection < string > list = new arraylist <> (); list . add ( \"apple\" ); list . add ( \"banana\" ); system . out . println ( list . size ()); // 2 collections hold objects , so primitives get boxed ( arraylist<integer> , not arraylist<int> ). most collection classes are cloneable and serializable , and all are iterable (you can loop over them)."}, {"id": "generics", "title": "Generics", "src": "cheat sheet, Ch. 20", "idea": "The type in angle brackets, like ArrayList<String>, tells the compiler what a collection holds. It catches wrong types at compile time and saves you from casting.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// &lt;&gt; \"diamond\": type inferred</span>\n<span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Noah\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// compile error: not a String</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">names</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// no cast needed</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Writing your own generic class</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Box</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">set</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">get</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Box</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Box</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">set</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> is a <strong>type parameter</strong>, a placeholder filled in when you use the class.</li>\n<li>Several are allowed: <code>class Pair&lt;A, B&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li>Bounded: <code>&lt;T extends Comparable&lt;T&gt;&gt;</code> means T must be comparable.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "arraylist < string > names = new arraylist <> (); // <> \"diamond\": type inferred names . add ( \"noah\" ); names . add ( 42 ); // compile error: not a string string first = names . get ( 0 ); // no cast needed writing your own generic class public class box < t > { private t value ; public void set ( t value ) { this . value = value ; } public t get () { return value ; } } box < integer > b = new box <> (); b . set ( 5 ); t is a type parameter , a placeholder filled in when you use the class. several are allowed: class pair<a, b> . bounded: <t extends comparable<t>> means t must be comparable."}, {"id": "iterating", "title": "Looping through collections", "src": "Ch. 20", "idea": "Three ways to visit every element: an Iterator (which can also remove items safely), a for-each loop (simplest), or forEach with a lambda.", "deep": "<p><strong>Iterator</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Iterator</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">iterator</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">hasNext</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">next</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">isEmpty</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">remove</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// safe removal while looping</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hasNext()</code></td>\n<td>more elements left?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>next()</code></td>\n<td>returns the next element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remove()</code></td>\n<td>removes the last one returned</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>For-each loop</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>forEach with a lambda</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">forEach</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> removing from a list inside a for-each loop throws <code>ConcurrentModificationException</code>. Use an Iterator's <code>remove()</code> or <code>list.removeIf(...)</code>. <span class=\"by\">Added by Fern</span></p>\n</blockquote>", "text": "iterator iterator < string > it = list . iterator (); while ( it . hasnext ()) { string item = it . next (); if ( item . isempty ()) it . remove (); // safe removal while looping } method does hasnext() more elements left? next() returns the next element remove() removes the last one returned for-each loop for ( string item : list ) { system . out . println ( item ); } foreach with a lambda list . foreach ( e -> system . out . println ( e )); heads up: removing from a list inside a for-each loop throws concurrentmodificationexception . use an iterator's remove() or list.removeif(...) . added by fern"}, {"id": "lists", "title": "Lists: ArrayList and LinkedList", "src": "Ch. 20, learning plan", "idea": "A List keeps elements in order, allows duplicates, and lets you reach items by index. ArrayList is fast for reading by index; LinkedList is better when you add and remove at the ends a lot.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Study Java\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Review notes\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"Study Java\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">set</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Updated task\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">remove</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">size</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tasks</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">contains</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Study Java\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>ArrayList</th>\n<th>LinkedList</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Built on</td>\n<td>resizable array</td>\n<td>linked nodes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Get by index</td>\n<td>fast</td>\n<td>slow</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Insert/remove in the middle</td>\n<td>slower</td>\n<td>faster (once you're there)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory</td>\n<td>less</td>\n<td>more</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Use when</td>\n<td>mostly reading, index access</td>\n<td>lots of adding/removing at the ends</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Vector vs ArrayList</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Vector</th>\n<th>ArrayList</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Thread-safe</td>\n<td>Yes (synchronized)</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speed</td>\n<td>Slower</td>\n<td>Faster</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Used today</td>\n<td>Rarely</td>\n<td>Commonly</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "arraylist < string > tasks = new arraylist <> (); tasks . add ( \"study java\" ); tasks . add ( \"review notes\" ); tasks . get ( 0 ); // \"study java\" tasks . set ( 0 , \"updated task\" ); tasks . remove ( 1 ); tasks . size (); tasks . contains ( \"study java\" ); arraylist linkedlist built on resizable array linked nodes get by index fast slow insert/remove in the middle slower faster (once you're there) memory less more use when mostly reading, index access lots of adding/removing at the ends vector vs arraylist vector arraylist thread-safe yes (synchronized) no speed slower faster used today rarely commonly"}, {"id": "collections-class", "title": "The Collections utility class", "src": "Ch. 20, Ch. 21", "idea": "Collections (with an s) is a class of static helper methods: sort, shuffle, max, min, binary search, plus ways to make read-only collections.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.sort(list)</code></td>\n<td>sorts (natural order)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.sort(list, comparator)</code></td>\n<td>sorts by a rule</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.shuffle(list)</code></td>\n<td>random order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.max(list)</code> / <code>min(list)</code></td>\n<td>largest / smallest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.binarySearch(list, key)</code></td>\n<td>searches a sorted list</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Collections.reverse(list)</code></td>\n<td>reverses in place</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Read-only collections</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">safe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Collections</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">unmodifiableList</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">original</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">safe</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"x\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// throws UnsupportedOperationException</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Collections</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">singleton</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// exactly one element</span>\n<span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fixed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">of</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"a\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"b\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"c\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// also unmodifiable</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Use these to prevent accidental changes.</p>", "text": "method does collections.sort(list) sorts (natural order) collections.sort(list, comparator) sorts by a rule collections.shuffle(list) random order collections.max(list) / min(list) largest / smallest collections.binarysearch(list, key) searches a sorted list collections.reverse(list) reverses in place read-only collections list < string > safe = collections . unmodifiablelist ( original ); safe . add ( \"x\" ); // throws unsupportedoperationexception set < string > one = collections . singleton ( \"a\" ); // exactly one element list < string > fixed = list . of ( \"a\" , \"b\" , \"c\" ); // also unmodifiable use these to prevent accidental changes."}, {"id": "stacks", "title": "Stacks", "src": "Ch. 20", "idea": "A stack is last-in, first-out (LIFO), like a stack of plates: you push onto the top and pop off the top.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Stack</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Stack</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">push</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">peek</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 3 (looks, doesn't remove)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pop</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// 3</span>\n<span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pop</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// 2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>push(x)</code></td>\n<td>add to the top</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pop()</code></td>\n<td>remove and return the top</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>peek()</code></td>\n<td>look at the top</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>empty()</code></td>\n<td>is it empty?</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Stack</code> extends <code>Vector</code>. (Modern code often uses <code>ArrayDeque</code> as a stack.)</li>\n<li>Stacks are used for <strong>evaluating expressions</strong>, <strong>checking matching brackets</strong>, undo, and parsing.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluating <code>(2 + 3) * 5</code> with two stacks:</strong> push numbers onto an operand stack and operators onto an operator stack; when an operator should be applied, pop two numbers and one operator, compute, and push the result back.</p>", "text": "stack < integer > stack = new stack <> (); stack . push ( 1 ); stack . push ( 2 ); stack . push ( 3 ); stack . peek (); // 3 (looks, doesn't remove) stack . pop (); // 3 stack . pop (); // 2 method does push(x) add to the top pop() remove and return the top peek() look at the top empty() is it empty? stack extends vector . (modern code often uses arraydeque as a stack.) stacks are used for evaluating expressions , checking matching brackets , undo, and parsing. evaluating (2 + 3) * 5 with two stacks: push numbers onto an operand stack and operators onto an operator stack; when an operator should be applied, pop two numbers and one operator, compute, and push the result back."}, {"id": "queues", "title": "Queues and priority queues", "src": "Ch. 20", "idea": "A queue is first-in, first-out (FIFO), like a line at a store. A priority queue instead always removes the smallest (highest-priority) element next.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Queue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinkedList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">offer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">offer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"B\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">offer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"C\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">poll</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"A\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">queue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">peek</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// \"B\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>offer(x)</code></td>\n<td>add to the back</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>poll()</code></td>\n<td>remove the front (null if empty)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>peek()</code></td>\n<td>look at the front</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remove()</code> / <code>element()</code></td>\n<td>like poll/peek, but throw if empty</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>PriorityQueue</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">poll</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// 1, then 3, then 5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Uses natural ordering (<code>Comparable</code>) or a <code>Comparator</code> you pass in:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">byLength</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "queue < string > queue = new linkedlist <> (); queue . offer ( \"a\" ); queue . offer ( \"b\" ); queue . offer ( \"c\" ); queue . poll (); // \"a\" queue . peek (); // \"b\" method does offer(x) add to the back poll() remove the front (null if empty) peek() look at the front remove() / element() like poll/peek, but throw if empty priorityqueue priorityqueue < integer > pq = new priorityqueue <> (); pq . add ( 5 ); pq . add ( 1 ); pq . add ( 3 ); pq . poll (); // 1, then 3, then 5 uses natural ordering ( comparable ) or a comparator you pass in: priorityqueue < string > bylength = new priorityqueue <> (( x , y ) -> x . length () - y . length ());"}, {"id": "sets", "title": "Sets", "src": "Ch. 21", "idea": "A Set stores unique elements only (duplicates are ignored) and has no index positions. HashSet is fastest, LinkedHashSet keeps insertion order, and TreeSet keeps items sorted.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// ignored</span>\n<span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">contains</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// true, and fast</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sorted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">of</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sorted</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// [1, 2, 3]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Set</th>\n<th>Order</th>\n<th>Speed</th>\n<th>Use when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>HashSet</code></td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>fastest</td>\n<td>general use</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>LinkedHashSet</code></td>\n<td>insertion order</td>\n<td>a bit slower</td>\n<td>order matters</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TreeSet</code></td>\n<td>sorted</td>\n<td>slowest</td>\n<td>you need sorted data</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Set</th>\n<th>List</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Duplicates</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Order</td>\n<td>depends on type</td>\n<td>always ordered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Index access</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>contains()</code> speed</td>\n<td>fast (hashing)</td>\n<td>slow (checks each one)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Remember:</strong> Hash = fast · Linked = keeps order · Tree = sorted.</p>\n<p><strong>Example: counting Java keywords in a file</strong> — put the keywords in a <code>HashSet</code>, read the file word by word, and count each word the set <code>contains()</code>.</p>", "text": "set < string > set = new hashset <> (); set . add ( \"a\" ); set . add ( \"a\" ); // ignored set . contains ( \"a\" ); // true, and fast set < integer > sorted = new treeset <> ( list . of ( 3 , 1 , 2 )); system . out . println ( sorted ); // [1, 2, 3] set order speed use when hashset none fastest general use linkedhashset insertion order a bit slower order matters treeset sorted slowest you need sorted data set list duplicates no yes order depends on type always ordered index access no yes contains() speed fast (hashing) slow (checks each one) remember: hash = fast · linked = keeps order · tree = sorted. example: counting java keywords in a file — put the keywords in a hashset , read the file word by word, and count each word the set contains() ."}, {"id": "maps", "title": "Maps", "src": "Ch. 21, learning plan", "idea": "A Map stores key → value pairs. Keys are unique (like a dictionary word); values can repeat. You look values up by key.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Map</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grades</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grades</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">put</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Alex\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">90</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grades</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">put</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Taylor\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">85</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grades</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Alex\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// 90</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grades</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">containsKey</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Sam\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">// false</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Map</th>\n<th>Order</th>\n<th>Speed</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>HashMap</code></td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>fastest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>LinkedHashMap</code></td>\n<td>insertion (or access) order</td>\n<td>medium</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TreeMap</code></td>\n<td>sorted by key</td>\n<td>slowest</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>put(k, v)</code></td>\n<td>add or replace</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>get(k)</code></td>\n<td>value for k (null if missing)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>getOrDefault(k, d)</code></td>\n<td>value, or d if missing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remove(k)</code></td>\n<td>removes the pair</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>containsKey(k)</code></td>\n<td>key present?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>keySet()</code></td>\n<td>all keys</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>values()</code></td>\n<td>all values</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>entrySet()</code></td>\n<td>all key-value pairs</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>The most-tested pattern: counting words</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Map</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">words</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">counts</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">put</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counts</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getOrDefault</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">word</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Map</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">Entry</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counts</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">entrySet</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getKey</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\": \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getValue</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Collection</th>\n<th>Map</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Stores</td>\n<td>single elements</td>\n<td>key-value pairs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Duplicate keys</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>not allowed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "map < string , integer > grades = new hashmap <> (); grades . put ( \"alex\" , 90 ); grades . put ( \"taylor\" , 85 ); grades . get ( \"alex\" ); // 90 grades . containskey ( \"sam\" ); // false map order speed hashmap none fastest linkedhashmap insertion (or access) order medium treemap sorted by key slowest method does put(k, v) add or replace get(k) value for k (null if missing) getordefault(k, d) value, or d if missing remove(k) removes the pair containskey(k) key present? keyset() all keys values() all values entryset() all key-value pairs the most-tested pattern: counting words map < string , integer > counts = new hashmap <> (); for ( string word : words ) { counts . put ( word , counts . getordefault ( word , 0 ) + 1 ); } for ( map . entry < string , integer > e : counts . entryset ()) { system . out . println ( e . getkey () + \": \" + e . getvalue ()); } collection map stores single elements key-value pairs duplicate keys — not allowed"}, {"id": "choosing-collection", "title": "Choosing a collection", "src": "learning plan, Ch. 21", "idea": "Pick by what you need: an ordered list with duplicates (ArrayList), unique items (HashSet), lookup by key (HashMap), last-in-first-out (stack) or first-in-first-out (queue).", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>You need…</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>ordered items, duplicates OK, access by index</td>\n<td><code>ArrayList</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>lots of adds/removes at both ends</td>\n<td><code>LinkedList</code> or <code>ArrayDeque</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>no duplicates, fast \"is it in there?\"</td>\n<td><code>HashSet</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>no duplicates, kept sorted</td>\n<td><code>TreeSet</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>look up a value by key</td>\n<td><code>HashMap</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>keys kept sorted</td>\n<td><code>TreeMap</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>last in, first out</td>\n<td><code>Stack</code> / <code>ArrayDeque</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>first in, first out</td>\n<td><code>Queue</code> (<code>LinkedList</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>always take the smallest/most urgent next</td>\n<td><code>PriorityQueue</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "you need… use ordered items, duplicates ok, access by index arraylist lots of adds/removes at both ends linkedlist or arraydeque no duplicates, fast \"is it in there?\" hashset no duplicates, kept sorted treeset look up a value by key hashmap keys kept sorted treemap last in, first out stack / arraydeque first in, first out queue ( linkedlist ) always take the smallest/most urgent next priorityqueue"}]}, {"id": "javafx", "title": "JavaFX", "blurb": "Building GUIs: windows, layouts, shapes, controls, events and animation.", "topics": [{"id": "javafx-intro", "title": "What JavaFX is", "src": "Ch. 14", "idea": "JavaFX is Java's modern toolkit for graphical user interfaces. It replaced the older AWT and Swing, and adds CSS-style styling, animation and media.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>AWT</th>\n<th>Swing</th>\n<th>JavaFX</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Age</td>\n<td>oldest</td>\n<td>older</td>\n<td>modern</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Components</td>\n<td>heavyweight</td>\n<td>lightweight</td>\n<td>modern UI toolkit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Styling</td>\n<td>limited</td>\n<td>moderate</td>\n<td>CSS-style</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graphics/animation</td>\n<td>basic</td>\n<td>better</td>\n<td>advanced</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Media</td>\n<td>minimal</td>\n<td>limited</td>\n<td>built in</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Use today?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>sometimes</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Fixing \"Module javafx.controls not found\"</strong> (add these VM options in IntelliJ's run configuration):</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>--module-path /path/to/javafx-sdk/lib --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "awt swing javafx age oldest older modern components heavyweight lightweight modern ui toolkit styling limited moderate css-style graphics/animation basic better advanced media minimal limited built in use today? no sometimes yes fixing \"module javafx.controls not found\" (add these vm options in intellij's run configuration): --module-path /path/to/javafx-sdk/lib --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml"}, {"id": "stage-scene-node", "title": "Stage, Scene and Nodes", "src": "Ch. 14", "idea": "A JavaFX app is nested boxes: the Stage is the window, the Scene is the content inside it, and Nodes are everything you see (panes, buttons, shapes, text).", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>Stage (window)\n └── Scene\n      └── Root node (a Pane)\n           ├── Button\n           ├── Text\n           └── Circle\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">javafx.application.Application</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">javafx.scene.Scene</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">javafx.scene.control.Button</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">javafx.scene.layout.StackPane</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">javafx.stage.Stage</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">HelloFX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Application</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">start</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Stage</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">primaryStage</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Button</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">btn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Button</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Click Me\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">StackPane</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">root</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StackPane</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">root</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getChildren</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">btn</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">Scene</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scene</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scene</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">root</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">300</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">200</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">primaryStage</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setTitle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"JavaFX App\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">primaryStage</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setScene</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">scene</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">primaryStage</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">show</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">launch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Every app <strong>extends <code>Application</code></strong> and <strong>overrides <code>start(Stage)</code></strong>.</li>\n<li>The <strong>primary stage</strong> is created for you by the JavaFX runtime.</li>\n<li><code>getChildren().add(node)</code> puts a node inside a pane.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common mistakes:</strong> forgetting <code>launch(args)</code>, forgetting <code>primaryStage.show()</code> (no window appears), importing Swing classes instead of <code>javafx...</code>.</p>", "text": "stage (window) └── scene └── root node (a pane) ├── button ├── text └── circle import javafx.application.application ; import javafx.scene.scene ; import javafx.scene.control.button ; import javafx.scene.layout.stackpane ; import javafx.stage.stage ; public class hellofx extends application { @override public void start ( stage primarystage ) { button btn = new button ( \"click me\" ); stackpane root = new stackpane (); root . getchildren (). add ( btn ); scene scene = new scene ( root , 300 , 200 ); primarystage . settitle ( \"javafx app\" ); primarystage . setscene ( scene ); primarystage . show (); } public static void main ( string [] args ) { launch ( args ); } } every app extends application and overrides start(stage) . the primary stage is created for you by the javafx runtime. getchildren().add(node) puts a node inside a pane. common mistakes: forgetting launch(args) , forgetting primarystage.show() (no window appears), importing swing classes instead of javafx... ."}, {"id": "layout-panes", "title": "Layout panes", "src": "Ch. 14", "idea": "Panes are containers that arrange their child nodes for you. Pick one by the layout you want: a row (HBox), a column (VBox), a grid (GridPane), regions (BorderPane) and so on.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Pane</th>\n<th>Arranges children</th>\n<th>Best for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Pane</code></td>\n<td>where you place them (<code>setLayoutX/Y</code>)</td>\n<td>manual positioning, drawings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>StackPane</code></td>\n<td>on top of each other, centered</td>\n<td>centering, overlays</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FlowPane</code></td>\n<td>left to right, wrapping</td>\n<td>wrapping rows of items</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>GridPane</code></td>\n<td>rows and columns</td>\n<td>forms, boards</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BorderPane</code></td>\n<td>top, bottom, left, right, center</td>\n<td>whole-app layouts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>HBox</code></td>\n<td>one horizontal row</td>\n<td>toolbars, button rows</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>VBox</code></td>\n<td>one vertical column</td>\n<td>stacked fields</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">GridPane</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GridPane</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grid</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">label</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// column 0, row 0</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grid</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">field</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">BorderPane</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">border</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BorderPane</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">border</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setTop</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">title</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">border</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setCenter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">HBox</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HBox</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">// 10px spacing</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "pane arranges children best for pane where you place them ( setlayoutx/y ) manual positioning, drawings stackpane on top of each other, centered centering, overlays flowpane left to right, wrapping wrapping rows of items gridpane rows and columns forms, boards borderpane top, bottom, left, right, center whole-app layouts hbox one horizontal row toolbars, button rows vbox one vertical column stacked fields gridpane grid = new gridpane (); grid . add ( label , 0 , 0 ); // column 0, row 0 grid . add ( field , 1 , 0 ); borderpane border = new borderpane (); border . settop ( title ); border . setcenter ( content ); hbox row = new hbox ( 10 ); // 10px spacing"}, {"id": "shapes-text", "title": "Shapes, text, colors, fonts and images", "src": "Ch. 14", "idea": "JavaFX has ready-made node classes for drawing: shapes like Circle and Rectangle, Text for words, Color and Font for styling, and ImageView for pictures.", "deep": "<p><strong>Shapes</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Line</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Rectangle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rect</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rectangle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Ellipse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ellipse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ellipse</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Polygon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tri</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polygon</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tri</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getPoints</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">addAll</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">50.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">100.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">100.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">100.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Text, color and font</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Text</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Text</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello JavaFX\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">circle</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setFill</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">BLUE</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">color</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.7</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// red, green, blue (0.0–1.0), optional opacity</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setFont</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Font</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">font</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Arial\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FontWeight</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">BOLD</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FontPosture</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">ITALIC</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Images</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Image</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">image</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Image</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file:image.png\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ImageView</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">view</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ImageView</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">image</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">view</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setFitWidth</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">200</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">view</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setFitHeight</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Node properties every node has</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setRotate</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">45</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">                                </span><span class=\"c1\">// degrees</span>\n<span class=\"n\">button</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setStyle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"-fx-background-color: blue;\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// CSS-style</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>ClockPane</strong> (textbook example): a reusable custom component that extends <code>Pane</code> and draws a circle, hands and numbers. Shows how to package custom graphics as a class.</p>", "text": "shapes line line = new line ( 0 , 0 , 100 , 100 ); circle circle = new circle ( 50 ); rectangle rect = new rectangle ( 100 , 50 ); ellipse ellipse = new ellipse ( 50 , 30 ); polygon tri = new polygon (); tri . getpoints (). addall ( 50.0 , 0.0 , 100.0 , 100.0 , 0.0 , 100.0 ); text, color and font text text = new text ( 50 , 50 , \"hello javafx\" ); circle . setfill ( color . blue ); color custom = color . color ( 0.5 , 0.2 , 0.7 ); // red, green, blue (0.0–1.0), optional opacity text . setfont ( font . font ( \"arial\" , fontweight . bold , fontposture . italic , 20 )); images image image = new image ( \"file:image.png\" ); imageview view = new imageview ( image ); view . setfitwidth ( 200 ); view . setfitheight ( 100 ); node properties every node has node . setrotate ( 45 ); // degrees button . setstyle ( \"-fx-background-color: blue;\" ); // css-style clockpane (textbook example): a reusable custom component that extends pane and draws a circle, hands and numbers. shows how to package custom graphics as a class."}, {"id": "binding", "title": "Properties and binding", "src": "Ch. 14, Ch. 15", "idea": "JavaFX values like a node's position are observable properties. Binding links one property to another, so when the source changes, the bound one updates automatically.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">// unidirectional: the circle's center follows the pane's size</span>\n<span class=\"n\">circle</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">centerXProperty</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">bind</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pane</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">widthProperty</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">divide</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">xProperty</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">bind</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">slider</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">valueProperty</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// bidirectional: each updates the other</span>\n<span class=\"n\">property1</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">bindBidirectional</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">property2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Every property has three methods</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>getText()</code></td>\n<td>the value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setText(\"Hi\")</code></td>\n<td>sets the value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>textProperty()</code></td>\n<td>the property object (needed for binding and listeners)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Observable objects and listeners:</strong> a listener runs code whenever a property changes.</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">slider</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">valueProperty</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">addListener</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">obs</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">oldVal</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newVal</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Now \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newVal</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">property</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">addListener</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">observable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// InvalidationListener</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Value changed\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "// unidirectional: the circle's center follows the pane's size circle . centerxproperty (). bind ( pane . widthproperty (). divide ( 2 )); text . xproperty (). bind ( slider . valueproperty ()); // bidirectional: each updates the other property1 . bindbidirectional ( property2 ); every property has three methods method returns gettext() the value settext(\"hi\") sets the value textproperty() the property object (needed for binding and listeners) observable objects and listeners: a listener runs code whenever a property changes. slider . valueproperty (). addlistener (( obs , oldval , newval ) -> { system . out . println ( \"now \" + newval ); }); property . addlistener ( observable -> { // invalidationlistener system . out . println ( \"value changed\" ); });"}, {"id": "events", "title": "Event-driven programming", "src": "Ch. 15", "idea": "A GUI program waits for the user to do something. Each action (a click, a key press) fires an event from a source node, and a handler you registered runs in response.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Traditional program</th>\n<th>Event-driven program</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>runs top to bottom</td>\n<td>waits for user actions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>input usually first</td>\n<td>input can happen anytime</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>focus on logic flow</td>\n<td>focus on handling events</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Flow:</strong> user acts → the <strong>event source</strong> (a Button, a Scene) fires → an <strong>event object</strong> is created → your <strong>handler</strong> runs.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Event class</th>\n<th>For</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ActionEvent</code></td>\n<td>button clicks, Enter in a TextField, ComboBox picks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>MouseEvent</code></td>\n<td>mouse actions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>KeyEvent</code></td>\n<td>keyboard</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>WindowEvent</code></td>\n<td>window actions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>All extend <code>javafx.event.Event</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Registering a handler</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">btOK</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Clicked\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>The <strong>event object</strong> carries details: which key, mouse coordinates, which button.</p>", "text": "traditional program event-driven program runs top to bottom waits for user actions input usually first input can happen anytime focus on logic flow focus on handling events flow: user acts → the event source (a button, a scene) fires → an event object is created → your handler runs. event class for actionevent button clicks, enter in a textfield, combobox picks mouseevent mouse actions keyevent keyboard windowevent window actions all extend javafx.event.event . registering a handler btok . setonaction ( e -> system . out . println ( \"clicked\" )); the event object carries details: which key, mouse coordinates, which button."}, {"id": "handlers-lambdas", "title": "Handlers: inner classes, anonymous classes and lambdas", "src": "Ch. 15", "idea": "A handler is an object implementing EventHandler. You can write it as a named inner class, an anonymous class, or, shortest of all, a lambda expression.", "deep": "<p><strong>Inner class</strong> (named, defined inside another class; can use the outer class's fields)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">OKHandler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EventHandler</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">ActionEvent</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">handle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ActionEvent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Clicked\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">btOK</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OKHandler</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Anonymous inner class</strong> (no name, written on the spot)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">btOK</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EventHandler</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">ActionEvent</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">handle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ActionEvent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Clicked\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Lambda expression</strong> (the modern way)</p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">btOK</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Clicked\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Inner class</th>\n<th>Anonymous class</th>\n<th>Lambda</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Has a name</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Separate definition</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shortest</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Functional interface (SAM):</strong> an interface with exactly <strong>one</strong> abstract method. Lambdas only work with these. <code>EventHandler</code> has one: <code>handle</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Lambda syntax:</strong> <code>(params) -&gt; expression</code> or <code>(params) -&gt; { statements }</code>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "inner class (named, defined inside another class; can use the outer class's fields) class okhandler implements eventhandler < actionevent > { @override public void handle ( actionevent e ) { system . out . println ( \"clicked\" ); } } btok . setonaction ( new okhandler ()); anonymous inner class (no name, written on the spot) btok . setonaction ( new eventhandler < actionevent > () { @override public void handle ( actionevent e ) { system . out . println ( \"clicked\" ); } }); lambda expression (the modern way) btok . setonaction ( e -> { system . out . println ( \"clicked\" ); }); inner class anonymous class lambda has a name yes no no separate definition yes no no shortest no no yes functional interface (sam): an interface with exactly one abstract method. lambdas only work with these. eventhandler has one: handle . lambda syntax: (params) -> expression or (params) -> { statements } ."}, {"id": "mouse-key-events", "title": "Mouse and key events", "src": "Ch. 15", "idea": "Mouse handlers tell you where and how the mouse was used; key handlers tell you which key. Attach key handlers to the scene (or a focused node).", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">pane</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnMouseClicked</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getX</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\", \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getY</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">scene</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnKeyPressed</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getCode</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KeyCode</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">UP</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"c1\">// move up</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Mouse method</th>\n<th>Fires when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnMouseClicked</code></td>\n<td>clicked</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnMousePressed</code> / <code>Released</code></td>\n<td>button down / up</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnMouseMoved</code></td>\n<td>moved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnMouseDragged</code></td>\n<td>moved with a button held</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Useful: <code>getX()</code>, <code>getY()</code>, <code>getButton()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Key method</th>\n<th>Fires when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnKeyPressed</code></td>\n<td>key goes down</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnKeyReleased</code></td>\n<td>key comes up</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnKeyTyped</code></td>\n<td>a character is typed</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Use <code>e.getCode()</code> for the key (<code>KeyCode.UP</code>, <code>KeyCode.A</code>…).</p>", "text": "pane . setonmouseclicked ( e -> { system . out . println ( e . getx () + \", \" + e . gety ()); }); scene . setonkeypressed ( e -> { if ( e . getcode () == keycode . up ) { // move up } }); mouse method fires when setonmouseclicked clicked setonmousepressed / released button down / up setonmousemoved moved setonmousedragged moved with a button held useful: getx() , gety() , getbutton() . key method fires when setonkeypressed key goes down setonkeyreleased key comes up setonkeytyped a character is typed use e.getcode() for the key ( keycode.up , keycode.a …)."}, {"id": "animation", "title": "Animation", "src": "Ch. 15", "idea": "JavaFX animation classes change a node over time. FadeTransition fades, PathTransition moves a node along a path, and Timeline runs any code at set intervals (like a bouncing ball).", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Class</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FadeTransition</code></td>\n<td>fades opacity in or out</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PathTransition</code></td>\n<td>moves a node along a path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Timeline</code></td>\n<td>runs keyframes over time (custom animations)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">FadeTransition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FadeTransition</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Duration</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">millis</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3000</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setFromValue</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setToValue</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setCycleCount</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Timeline</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">INDEFINITE</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setAutoReverse</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ft</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">play</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Bouncing ball with a Timeline</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Timeline</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">animation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Timeline</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KeyFrame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Duration</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">millis</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">moveBall</span><span class=\"p\">()));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">animation</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setCycleCount</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Timeline</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">INDEFINITE</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">animation</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">play</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// inside moveBall():</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">width</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">radius</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// hit a wall: reverse</span>\n<span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dx</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>Practices timing, position updates, collision detection and direction changes. The <strong>US map</strong> example practices shapes, coordinates, colors, binding and resizing.</p>\n<p><strong>Loan calculator GUI</strong> practices TextFields, Labels, a Button, layout and parsing input: <code>Double.parseDouble(tf.getText())</code>, then <code>lbl.setText(result)</code>.</p>", "text": "class does fadetransition fades opacity in or out pathtransition moves a node along a path timeline runs keyframes over time (custom animations) fadetransition ft = new fadetransition ( duration . millis ( 3000 ), text ); ft . setfromvalue ( 1.0 ); ft . settovalue ( 0.1 ); ft . setcyclecount ( timeline . indefinite ); ft . setautoreverse ( true ); ft . play (); bouncing ball with a timeline timeline animation = new timeline ( new keyframe ( duration . millis ( 50 ), e -> moveball ())); animation . setcyclecount ( timeline . indefinite ); animation . play (); // inside moveball(): if ( x < radius || x > width - radius ) dx *= - 1 ; // hit a wall: reverse x += dx ; practices timing, position updates, collision detection and direction changes. the us map example practices shapes, coordinates, colors, binding and resizing. loan calculator gui practices textfields, labels, a button, layout and parsing input: double.parsedouble(tf.gettext()) , then lbl.settext(result) ."}, {"id": "ui-controls", "title": "UI controls", "src": "Ch. 16", "idea": "Controls are the interactive pieces: buttons, check boxes, text fields, drop-downs, lists and sliders. Create one, add it to a pane, then attach a handler or listener.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Control</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Label</code></td>\n<td>shows text or an image</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Button</code></td>\n<td>does something when clicked</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CheckBox</code></td>\n<td>on/off; several can be selected</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RadioButton</code></td>\n<td>pick exactly one (needs a <code>ToggleGroup</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TextField</code></td>\n<td>one line of input</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PasswordField</code></td>\n<td>hidden input (<code>******</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TextArea</code></td>\n<td>multi-line input</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ComboBox&lt;T&gt;</code></td>\n<td>drop-down, pick one</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ListView&lt;T&gt;</code></td>\n<td>list, pick one or many</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ScrollBar</code></td>\n<td>scrolling or picking a value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Slider</code></td>\n<td>picking a value, with ticks and labels</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">CheckBox</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">chkBold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CheckBox</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Bold\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">chkBold</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">chkBold</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">isSelected</span><span class=\"p\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cm\">/* ... */</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">RadioButton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rbRed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RadioButton</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Red\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">RadioButton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rbBlue</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RadioButton</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Blue\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ToggleGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ToggleGroup</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rbRed</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setToggleGroup</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">group</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// without a group, both can be on</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rbBlue</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setToggleGroup</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">group</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">TextField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tfName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TextField</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">tfName</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tfName</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getText</span><span class=\"p\">()));</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// fires on Enter</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">ComboBox</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">combo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ComboBox</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">combo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getItems</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">addAll</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Red\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Blue\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Green\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">combo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setOnAction</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">combo</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getValue</span><span class=\"p\">()));</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">ListView</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ListView</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lv</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getItems</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">addAll</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Apple\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Banana\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Orange\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lv</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getSelectionModel</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"na\">setSelectionMode</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SelectionMode</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">MULTIPLE</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Slider</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">slider</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Slider</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// min, max, start</span>\n<span class=\"n\">slider</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setShowTickMarks</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">slider</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setShowTickLabels</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p><strong>Label extras:</strong> <code>setGraphic()</code>, <code>setTextFill()</code>, <code>setFont()</code>, <code>setUnderline(true)</code>, <code>setWrapText(true)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Slider vs ScrollBar:</strong> a Slider is more visual (ticks, labels) and suits settings; a ScrollBar usually scrolls content.</p>\n<p><strong>The control family tree</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Base class</th>\n<th>Gives</th>\n<th>Used by</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Labeled</code></td>\n<td>text, graphic, alignment, wrapping</td>\n<td>Label, Button, CheckBox, RadioButton</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ButtonBase</code></td>\n<td><code>onAction</code></td>\n<td>Button, CheckBox, RadioButton</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TextInputControl</code></td>\n<td>text, editable</td>\n<td>TextField, TextArea</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ComboBox</code> and <code>ListView</code> store items in an <strong>ObservableList</strong>, which updates the UI when the data changes: <code>FXCollections.observableArrayList()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tic-tac-toe</strong> (textbook example): a <code>GridPane</code> of clickable cells; each click marks X or O, checks for a winner, and switches turns.</p>", "text": "control purpose label shows text or an image button does something when clicked checkbox on/off; several can be selected radiobutton pick exactly one (needs a togglegroup ) textfield one line of input passwordfield hidden input ( ****** ) textarea multi-line input combobox<t> drop-down, pick one listview<t> list, pick one or many scrollbar scrolling or picking a value slider picking a value, with ticks and labels checkbox chkbold = new checkbox ( \"bold\" ); chkbold . setonaction ( e -> { if ( chkbold . isselected ()) { /* ... */ } }); radiobutton rbred = new radiobutton ( \"red\" ); radiobutton rbblue = new radiobutton ( \"blue\" ); togglegroup group = new togglegroup (); rbred . settogglegroup ( group ); // without a group, both can be on rbblue . settogglegroup ( group ); textfield tfname = new textfield (); tfname . setonaction ( e -> system . out . println ( tfname . gettext ())); // fires on enter combobox < string > combo = new combobox <> (); combo . getitems (). addall ( \"red\" , \"blue\" , \"green\" ); combo . setonaction ( e -> system . out . println ( combo . getvalue ())); listview < string > lv = new listview <> (); lv . getitems (). addall ( \"apple\" , \"banana\" , \"orange\" ); lv . getselectionmodel (). setselectionmode ( selectionmode . multiple ); slider slider = new slider ( 0 , 100 , 50 ); // min, max, start slider . setshowtickmarks ( true ); slider . setshowticklabels ( true ); label extras: setgraphic() , settextfill() , setfont() , setunderline(true) , setwraptext(true) . slider vs scrollbar: a slider is more visual (ticks, labels) and suits settings; a scrollbar usually scrolls content. the control family tree base class gives used by labeled text, graphic, alignment, wrapping label, button, checkbox, radiobutton buttonbase onaction button, checkbox, radiobutton textinputcontrol text, editable textfield, textarea combobox and listview store items in an observablelist , which updates the ui when the data changes: fxcollections.observablearraylist() . tic-tac-toe (textbook example): a gridpane of clickable cells; each click marks x or o, checks for a winner, and switches turns."}, {"id": "media", "title": "Audio and video", "src": "Ch. 16", "idea": "Three classes play media: Media loads the file, MediaPlayer controls playback, and MediaView displays video on screen.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Media</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">media</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Media</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fileURL</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">MediaPlayer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">player</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MediaPlayer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">media</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">MediaView</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">view</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MediaView</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">player</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">player</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">play</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">player</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">pause</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">player</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">stop</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>The <strong>flag and anthem</strong> case study combines images, media, buttons and layout.</p>", "text": "media media = new media ( fileurl ); mediaplayer player = new mediaplayer ( media ); mediaview view = new mediaview ( player ); player . play (); player . pause (); player . stop (); the flag and anthem case study combines images, media, buttons and layout."}]}, {"id": "concurrency-testing", "title": "Concurrency and testing", "blurb": "Running tasks at the same time safely, and checking code automatically.", "topics": [{"id": "threads", "title": "Threads and Runnable", "src": "learning plan", "idea": "A thread is a separate path of execution, so a program can work on several tasks at once. Put the task's code in a Runnable's run() method, then call start() on a Thread.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">MessageTask</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Runnable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">MessageTask</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">message</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">run</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MessageTask</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"First\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MessageTask</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Second\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// the two outputs interleave unpredictably</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Heads up:</strong> call <code>start()</code>, not <code>run()</code>. <code>start()</code> creates a new thread. Calling <code>run()</code> directly just runs the method on the current thread, one after the other.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li><code>thread.join()</code> waits for a thread to finish.</li>\n<li>A lambda works too: <code>new Thread(() -&gt; doWork()).start();</code></li>\n</ul>", "text": "public class messagetask implements runnable { private final string message ; public messagetask ( string message ) { this . message = message ; } @override public void run () { for ( int i = 0 ; i < 5 ; i ++ ) { system . out . println ( message ); } } } thread first = new thread ( new messagetask ( \"first\" )); thread second = new thread ( new messagetask ( \"second\" )); first . start (); second . start (); // the two outputs interleave unpredictably heads up: call start() , not run() . start() creates a new thread. calling run() directly just runs the method on the current thread, one after the other. thread.join() waits for a thread to finish. a lambda works too: new thread(() -> dowork()).start();"}, {"id": "synchronization", "title": "Race conditions and synchronization", "src": "learning plan", "idea": "When two threads change shared data at the same moment, updates can get lost: a race condition. synchronized lets only one thread at a time run that code on the same object.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Counter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">synchronized</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">increment</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// read, add, write: not safe without synchronized</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getValue</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Race condition:</strong> the result depends on the unpredictable timing of threads.</li>\n<li><strong>synchronized:</strong> a lock; one thread at a time per object.</li>\n<li>Too much synchronization slows things down.</li>\n<li><strong>Deadlock:</strong> two threads each hold a lock the other needs, so both wait forever.</li>\n<li><strong>Producer–consumer:</strong> a classic pattern where one thread adds items to a shared buffer and another removes them, coordinating with <code>wait()</code>/<code>notify()</code> or a <code>BlockingQueue</code>.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public class counter { private int value ; public synchronized void increment () { value ++ ; // read, add, write: not safe without synchronized } public int getvalue () { return value ; } } race condition: the result depends on the unpredictable timing of threads. synchronized: a lock; one thread at a time per object. too much synchronization slows things down. deadlock: two threads each hold a lock the other needs, so both wait forever. producer–consumer: a classic pattern where one thread adds items to a shared buffer and another removes them, coordinating with wait() / notify() or a blockingqueue ."}, {"id": "unit-testing", "title": "Unit testing with JUnit", "src": "learning plan", "idea": "A unit test is a small method that runs one piece of your code and checks the result automatically. Test normal cases, boundary cases and invalid input.", "deep": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">org.junit.jupiter.api.Test</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">CalculatorTest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Test</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">addsTwoPositives</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">assertEquals</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Calculator</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Test</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">rejectsNegativeAge</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">assertThrows</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IllegalArgumentException</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">class</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">person</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">setAge</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Assertion</th>\n<th>Passes when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>assertEquals(expected, actual)</code></td>\n<td>they're equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>assertTrue(condition)</code></td>\n<td>condition is true</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>assertFalse(condition)</code></td>\n<td>condition is false</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>assertNull(x)</code> / <code>assertNotNull(x)</code></td>\n<td>x is / isn't null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>assertThrows(Type.class, () -&gt; call())</code></td>\n<td>the call throws that exception</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Normal case:</strong> typical input. <strong>Boundary case:</strong> edges like 0, empty, max. <strong>Invalid input:</strong> things that should be rejected.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "public static int add ( int first , int second ) { return first + second ; } import static org.junit.jupiter.api.assertions.* ; import org.junit.jupiter.api.test ; public class calculatortest { @test public void addstwopositives () { assertequals ( 7 , calculator . add ( 3 , 4 )); } @test public void rejectsnegativeage () { assertthrows ( illegalargumentexception . class , () -> person . setage ( - 1 )); } } assertion passes when assertequals(expected, actual) they're equal asserttrue(condition) condition is true assertfalse(condition) condition is false assertnull(x) / assertnotnull(x) x is / isn't null assertthrows(type.class, () -> call()) the call throws that exception normal case: typical input. boundary case: edges like 0, empty, max. invalid input: things that should be rejected."}]}, {"id": "practice", "title": "Practice projects", "blurb": "Programs to build, from quick drills to full projects.", "topics": [{"id": "study-routine", "title": "How to practice", "src": "learning plan", "idea": "Learn one concept, then write the code yourself without copying, then record what broke and how you fixed it. Retyping from memory is where the learning sticks.", "deep": "<p><strong>A 90-minute session</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Time</th>\n<th>Do</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>15 min</td>\n<td>review the code from last time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>25 min</td>\n<td>learn one new concept (Dev.java or Oracle)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>40 min</td>\n<td>write code without copying the example, or do exercises</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10 min</td>\n<td>write down errors and what fixed them</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>For each topic:</strong> read the lesson, write the examples yourself, then do two or three related Exercism or MOOC.fi exercises.</p>\n<p><strong>Short on time? A 10-minute warm-up</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open one card on this page you haven't marked \"Got it\".</li>\n<li>Read the main idea, then the deeper notes.</li>\n<li>Close it and retype its code example from memory in IntelliJ.</li>\n<li>Run it. Fix what breaks.</li>\n</ol>", "text": "a 90-minute session time do 15 min review the code from last time 25 min learn one new concept (dev.java or oracle) 40 min write code without copying the example, or do exercises 10 min write down errors and what fixed them for each topic: read the lesson, write the examples yourself, then do two or three related exercism or mooc.fi exercises. short on time? a 10-minute warm-up open one card on this page you haven't marked \"got it\". read the main idea, then the deeper notes. close it and retype its code example from memory in intellij. run it. fix what breaks."}, {"id": "drills", "title": "Quick drills", "src": "Ch. 2, learning plan", "idea": "Small programs that each practice one skill. Good for warm-ups, or for rebuilding from memory to check that something stuck.", "deep": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Program</th>\n<th>Practices</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sum two numbers the user enters</td>\n<td>Scanner, doubles</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Minutes → hours and minutes</td>\n<td><code>/</code> and <code>%</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total cost after 6% tax</td>\n<td>constants, math</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Temperature converter</td>\n<td>variables, operators, casting</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Grade calculator</td>\n<td>if / else if / switch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multiplication table</td>\n<td>nested for loops</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Number-guessing game</td>\n<td>while loop, Random</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calculator split into methods</td>\n<td>methods, parameters, return</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Average, highest and lowest of an array</td>\n<td>arrays, for-each</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Count words, vowels and repeated characters</td>\n<td>String methods, loops</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Factorial, sum to n, reverse a string, count digits</td>\n<td>recursion</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Example: minutes to hours</strong></p>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">in</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Enter minutes: \"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">totalMinutes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">nextInt</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hours</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">totalMinutes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">60</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">minutes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">totalMinutes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">60</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hours</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" hours and \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">minutes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" minutes\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "program practices sum two numbers the user enters scanner, doubles minutes → hours and minutes / and % total cost after 6% tax constants, math temperature converter variables, operators, casting grade calculator if / else if / switch multiplication table nested for loops number-guessing game while loop, random calculator split into methods methods, parameters, return average, highest and lowest of an array arrays, for-each count words, vowels and repeated characters string methods, loops factorial, sum to n, reverse a string, count digits recursion example: minutes to hours scanner input = new scanner ( system . in ); system . out . print ( \"enter minutes: \" ); int totalminutes = input . nextint (); int hours = totalminutes / 60 ; int minutes = totalminutes % 60 ; system . out . println ( hours + \" hours and \" + minutes + \" minutes\" );"}, {"id": "projects", "title": "Bigger projects", "src": "learning plan, Ch. 15, Ch. 16", "idea": "Projects that combine several units. Each one has a clear checklist so you know when it's done.", "deep": "<p><strong>Grade analyzer</strong> (arrays + methods)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Store at least five grades in an array.</li>\n<li>Calculate the total and average.</li>\n<li>Find the highest and lowest.</li>\n<li>Print a letter grade for the average.</li>\n<li>Put each calculation in its own method.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Employee payroll system</strong> (inheritance + polymorphism)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Abstract <code>Employee</code> class with an abstract <code>calculatePay()</code>.</li>\n<li><code>HourlyEmployee</code> and <code>SalariedEmployee</code> subclasses that override it.</li>\n<li>An <code>ArrayList&lt;Employee&gt;</code> holding both kinds.</li>\n<li>A loop printing every employee's info and pay.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student record manager</strong> (collections + files + exceptions)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Menu: add a student, display all, search by ID or name, sort by GPA.</li>\n<li>Save records to a text file and load them at startup.</li>\n<li>Handle bad menu choices and invalid grades.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>JavaFX builds:</strong> login form, settings menu, tic-tac-toe board, media player, simple survey app, loan calculator.</p>", "text": "grade analyzer (arrays + methods) store at least five grades in an array. calculate the total and average. find the highest and lowest. print a letter grade for the average. put each calculation in its own method. employee payroll system (inheritance + polymorphism) abstract employee class with an abstract calculatepay() . hourlyemployee and salariedemployee subclasses that override it. an arraylist<employee> holding both kinds. a loop printing every employee's info and pay. student record manager (collections + files + exceptions) menu: add a student, display all, search by id or name, sort by gpa. save records to a text file and load them at startup. handle bad menu choices and invalid grades. javafx builds: login form, settings menu, tic-tac-toe board, media player, simple survey app, loan calculator."}, {"id": "final-project", "title": "Final project checklist", "src": "learning plan", "idea": "A capstone-style program that pulls everything together. Plan the classes first, then build, test and refactor.", "deep": "<p><strong>Ideas:</strong> expense tracker, library system, quiz app, text-based adventure, student grade manager, JavaFX task manager.</p>\n<p><strong>Before coding, answer</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>What problem does it solve, and what can the user do?</li>\n<li>Which classes do you need, and what is each responsible for?</li>\n<li>What data gets stored?</li>\n<li>Which invalid inputs must be handled?</li>\n<li>How will you test it?</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example class plan: expense tracker</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Class</th>\n<th>Responsibility</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Expense</code></td>\n<td>date, category, amount, description</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ExpenseManager</code></td>\n<td>add, remove, search, total</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FileManager</code></td>\n<td>save and load</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>InputValidator</code></td>\n<td>check dates, numbers, menu choices</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ExpenseTracker</code></td>\n<td>menu and program flow</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>At least four classes</li>\n<li>Encapsulation</li>\n<li>Inheritance or an interface where it makes sense</li>\n<li>An <code>ArrayList</code> or another collection</li>\n<li>Input validation and exception handling</li>\n<li>File reading and writing</li>\n<li>At least five unit tests</li>\n<li>Clear names, a short UML diagram, comments where the reasoning isn't obvious</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Order of work:</strong> design and UML → core classes → menu, validation, files → test and fix → refactor and write a short reflection.</p>", "text": "ideas: expense tracker, library system, quiz app, text-based adventure, student grade manager, javafx task manager. before coding, answer what problem does it solve, and what can the user do? which classes do you need, and what is each responsible for? what data gets stored? which invalid inputs must be handled? how will you test it? example class plan: expense tracker class responsibility expense date, category, amount, description expensemanager add, remove, search, total filemanager save and load inputvalidator check dates, numbers, menu choices expensetracker menu and program flow requirements at least four classes encapsulation inheritance or an interface where it makes sense an arraylist or another collection input validation and exception handling file reading and writing at least five unit tests clear names, a short uml diagram, comments where the reasoning isn't obvious order of work: design and uml → core classes → menu, validation, files → test and fix → refactor and write a short reflection."}]}], "ref": [{"id": "ref-commands", "title": "Compile and run", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code>javac<span class=\"w\"> </span>HelloWorld.java<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\"># compile → HelloWorld.class</span>\njava<span class=\"w\"> </span>HelloWorld<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"c1\"># run (no .class)</span>\njava<span class=\"w\"> </span>Test<span class=\"w\"> </span>hello<span class=\"w\"> </span>world<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\"># args[0] = \"hello\", args[1] = \"world\"</span>\njava<span class=\"w\"> </span>--module-path<span class=\"w\"> </span>/path/to/javafx-sdk/lib<span class=\"w\"> </span>--add-modules<span class=\"w\"> </span>javafx.controls<span class=\"w\"> </span>App\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">HelloWorld</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// print + new line</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"No newline\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">err</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Error output\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "javac helloworld.java # compile → helloworld.class java helloworld # run (no .class) java test hello world # args[0] = \"hello\", args[1] = \"world\" java --module-path /path/to/javafx-sdk/lib --add-modules javafx.controls app public class helloworld { public static void main ( string [] args ) { system . out . println ( \"hello\" ); // print + new line system . out . print ( \"no newline\" ); system . err . println ( \"error output\" ); } }"}, {"id": "ref-types", "title": "Types and literals", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Literal</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>byte</code></td>\n<td>8 bit</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n<td><code>(byte) 10</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>short</code></td>\n<td>16 bit</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n<td><code>300</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>int</code></td>\n<td>32 bit</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n<td><code>42</code>, <code>0x1AF</code>, <code>0b101</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>long</code></td>\n<td>64 bit</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n<td><code>8000000000L</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>float</code></td>\n<td>32 bit</td>\n<td><code>0.0</code></td>\n<td><code>98.6F</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>double</code></td>\n<td>64 bit</td>\n<td><code>0.0</code></td>\n<td><code>19.99</code>, <code>1.23e4</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>char</code></td>\n<td>16 bit</td>\n<td><code>'\\u0000'</code></td>\n<td><code>'A'</code>, <code>'\\n'</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td><code>false</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>objects</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n<td><code>\"text\"</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TAX_RATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.06</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"c1\">// constant</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">9.7</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">                         </span><span class=\"c1\">// 9 (cast)</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">parseInt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"123\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"c1\">// String → int</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Double</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">parseDouble</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"1.5\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// String → double</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">valueOf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"c1\">// anything → String</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "type size default literal byte 8 bit 0 (byte) 10 short 16 bit 0 300 int 32 bit 0 42 , 0x1af , 0b101 long 64 bit 0 8000000000l float 32 bit 0.0 98.6f double 64 bit 0.0 19.99 , 1.23e4 char 16 bit '\\u0000' 'a' , '\\n' boolean — false true objects — null \"text\" final double tax_rate = 0.06 ; // constant int y = ( int ) 9.7 ; // 9 (cast) int n = integer . parseint ( \"123\" ); // string → int double d = double . parsedouble ( \"1.5\" ); // string → double string s = string . valueof ( 42 ); // anything → string"}, {"id": "ref-operators", "title": "Operators", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Kind</th>\n<th>Operators</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Arithmetic</td>\n<td><code>+ - * / %</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assignment</td>\n<td><code>= += -= *= /= %=</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Increment</td>\n<td><code>++x x++ --x x--</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Relational</td>\n<td><code>== != &lt; &lt;= &gt; &gt;=</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Logical</td>\n<td><code>&amp;&amp;</code> (and) · <code>||</code> (or) · <code>!</code> (not) · <code>^</code> (xor)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ternary</td>\n<td><code>cond ? a : b</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bitwise</td>\n<td><code>&amp; | ^ ~ &lt;&lt; &gt;&gt; &gt;&gt;&gt;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Type check</td>\n<td><code>obj instanceof Type</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "kind operators arithmetic + - * / % assignment = += -= *= /= %= increment ++x x++ --x x-- relational == != < <= > >= logical && (and) · || (or) · ! (not) · ^ (xor) ternary cond ? a : b bitwise & | ^ ~ << >> >>> type check obj instanceof type"}, {"id": "ref-control", "title": "Control flow", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">switch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">...;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">default</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">...;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">switch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"one\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"other\"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cond</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">while</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cond</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">item</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collection</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// leave the loop</span>\n<span class=\"k\">continue</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// skip to the next pass</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "if ( a ) { } else if ( b ) { } else { } switch ( x ) { case 1 : ...; break ; default : ...; } string s = switch ( x ) { case 1 -> \"one\" ; default -> \"other\" ; }; while ( cond ) { } do { } while ( cond ); for ( int i = 0 ; i < n ; i ++ ) { } for ( type item : collection ) { } break ; // leave the loop continue ; // skip to the next pass"}, {"id": "ref-scanner", "title": "Scanner (keyboard and files)", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">java.util.Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">in</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">File</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"data.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextInt()</code> / <code>nextDouble()</code> / <code>nextLong()</code></td>\n<td>a number</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>next()</code></td>\n<td>one word</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nextLine()</code></td>\n<td>the rest of the line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>next().charAt(0)</code></td>\n<td>one character</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hasNext()</code> / <code>hasNextLine()</code> / <code>hasNextInt()</code></td>\n<td>is there more (of that type)?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>close()</code></td>\n<td>closes it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "import java.util.scanner ; scanner input = new scanner ( system . in ); scanner file = new scanner ( new file ( \"data.txt\" )); method returns nextint() / nextdouble() / nextlong() a number next() one word nextline() the rest of the line next().charat(0) one character hasnext() / hasnextline() / hasnextint() is there more (of that type)? close() closes it"}, {"id": "ref-strings", "title": "String methods", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>length()</code></td>\n<td>number of chars</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>charAt(i)</code></td>\n<td>char at index i</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>substring(b, e)</code></td>\n<td>chars b to e-1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>indexOf(s)</code> / <code>indexOf(s, from)</code> / <code>lastIndexOf(s)</code></td>\n<td>position or -1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>contains(s)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>startsWith(s)</code> / <code>endsWith(s)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>equals(s)</code> / <code>equalsIgnoreCase(s)</code></td>\n<td>same contents?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>compareTo(s)</code></td>\n<td>negative / 0 / positive</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>toUpperCase()</code> / <code>toLowerCase()</code></td>\n<td>new String</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>trim()</code> / <code>strip()</code></td>\n<td>without outer spaces</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>replace(a, b)</code> / <code>replaceAll(regex, b)</code></td>\n<td>new String</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>split(delim)</code></td>\n<td><code>String[]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>isEmpty()</code> / <code>isBlank()</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>String.join(\", \", list)</code></td>\n<td>joined String</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>String.format(\"%.2f\", x)</code></td>\n<td>formatted String</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>StringBuilder:</strong> <code>append(x)</code>, <code>insert(i, x)</code>, <code>delete(b, e)</code>, <code>reverse()</code>, <code>setCharAt(i, c)</code>, <code>toString()</code></p>", "text": "method returns length() number of chars charat(i) char at index i substring(b, e) chars b to e-1 indexof(s) / indexof(s, from) / lastindexof(s) position or -1 contains(s) boolean startswith(s) / endswith(s) boolean equals(s) / equalsignorecase(s) same contents? compareto(s) negative / 0 / positive touppercase() / tolowercase() new string trim() / strip() without outer spaces replace(a, b) / replaceall(regex, b) new string split(delim) string[] isempty() / isblank() boolean string.join(\", \", list) joined string string.format(\"%.2f\", x) formatted string stringbuilder: append(x) , insert(i, x) , delete(b, e) , reverse() , setcharat(i, c) , tostring()"}, {"id": "ref-format", "title": "printf and escape sequences", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Specifier</th>\n<th>For</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%d</code></td>\n<td>integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%f</code> / <code>%.2f</code></td>\n<td>decimal / 2 places</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%s</code></td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%c</code></td>\n<td>char</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%b</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%n</code></td>\n<td>new line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%8d</code>, <code>%-10s</code></td>\n<td>width (right / left aligned)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Escape</th>\n<th>Means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\n</code></td>\n<td>new line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\t</code></td>\n<td>tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\\\</code></td>\n<td>backslash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\\"</code></td>\n<td>double quote</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\\'</code></td>\n<td>single quote</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "specifier for %d integer %f / %.2f decimal / 2 places %s string %c char %b boolean %n new line %8d , %-10s width (right / left aligned) escape means \\n new line \\t tab \\\\ backslash \\\" double quote \\' single quote"}, {"id": "ref-math", "title": "Math and Character", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Math</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.pow(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>a^b (double)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.sqrt(x)</code></td>\n<td>√x (double)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.abs(x)</code></td>\n<td>absolute value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.max(a, b)</code> / <code>Math.min(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>larger / smaller</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.round(x)</code></td>\n<td>nearest whole (long/int)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.ceil(x)</code> / <code>Math.floor(x)</code></td>\n<td>up / down (double)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.random()</code></td>\n<td>0.0 to &lt;1.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.sin/cos/tan(rad)</code></td>\n<td>trig</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.toRadians(d)</code> / <code>Math.toDegrees(r)</code></td>\n<td>convert</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.log(x)</code></td>\n<td>natural log</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Math.PI</code></td>\n<td>π</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Character</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isDigit(c)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isLetter(c)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isLetterOrDigit(c)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.isUpperCase(c)</code> / <code>isLowerCase(c)</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Character.toUpperCase(c)</code> / <code>toLowerCase(c)</code></td>\n<td>char</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Random int in a range: <code>(int) (Math.random() * count) + start</code> or <code>new Random().nextInt(n)</code> (0 to n-1).</p>", "text": "math returns math.pow(a, b) a^b (double) math.sqrt(x) √x (double) math.abs(x) absolute value math.max(a, b) / math.min(a, b) larger / smaller math.round(x) nearest whole (long/int) math.ceil(x) / math.floor(x) up / down (double) math.random() 0.0 to <1.0 math.sin/cos/tan(rad) trig math.toradians(d) / math.todegrees(r) convert math.log(x) natural log math.pi π character returns character.isdigit(c) boolean character.isletter(c) boolean character.isletterordigit(c) boolean character.isuppercase(c) / islowercase(c) boolean character.touppercase(c) / tolowercase(c) char random int in a range: (int) (math.random() * count) + start or new random().nextint(n) (0 to n-1)."}, {"id": "ref-arrays", "title": "Arrays", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">};</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[][]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">rows</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">cols</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// field, no ()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">grid</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">length</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// columns in row r</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.sort(a)</code></td>\n<td>sort in place</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.binarySearch(a, key)</code></td>\n<td>index in a sorted array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.toString(a)</code></td>\n<td><code>\"[1, 2, 3]\"</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.equals(a, b)</code></td>\n<td>same contents?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.fill(a, v)</code></td>\n<td>set all to v</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arrays.copyOf(a, n)</code></td>\n<td>copy of length n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>System.arraycopy(src, sPos, dest, dPos, len)</code></td>\n<td>copy a range</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "int [] a = new int [ 5 ] ; int [] b = { 1 , 2 , 3 }; int [][] grid = new int [ rows ][ cols ] ; a . length ; // field, no () grid [ r ] . length ; // columns in row r method does arrays.sort(a) sort in place arrays.binarysearch(a, key) index in a sorted array arrays.tostring(a) \"[1, 2, 3]\" arrays.equals(a, b) same contents? arrays.fill(a, v) set all to v arrays.copyof(a, n) copy of length n system.arraycopy(src, spos, dest, dpos, len) copy a range"}, {"id": "ref-oop", "title": "Classes and OOP keywords", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Dog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Animal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">implements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pet</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Comparable</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Dog</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"c1\">// field</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"c1\">// shared field</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">final</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MAX</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"c1\">// constant</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">Dog</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"c1\">// constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">                            </span><span class=\"c1\">// superclass constructor (first line)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">this</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">toString</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dog: \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@Override</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">compareTo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Dog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">other</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">compareTo</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">other</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">abstract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">Shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">abstract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">getArea</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">interface</span> <span class=\"nc\">Flyable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">fly</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">record</span> <span class=\"nc\">Point</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Keyword</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>extends</code></td>\n<td>inherit from one class (or extend an interface)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>implements</code></td>\n<td>promise to provide an interface's methods</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>super</code> / <code>super.method()</code></td>\n<td>parent constructor / parent version</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>this</code> / <code>this(...)</code></td>\n<td>current object / another constructor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>abstract</code></td>\n<td>can't instantiate / method with no body</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>final</code></td>\n<td>can't change (variable), override (method), extend (class)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>static</code></td>\n<td>belongs to the class</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>private</code> / <code>protected</code> / <code>public</code></td>\n<td>class only / package + subclasses / everyone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>instanceof</code></td>\n<td>type check</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "public class dog extends animal implements pet , comparable < dog > { private string name ; // field private static int count ; // shared field public static final int max = 10 ; // constant public dog ( string name ) { // constructor super (); // superclass constructor (first line) this . name = name ; } @override public string tostring () { return \"dog: \" + name ; } @override public int compareto ( dog other ) { return name . compareto ( other . name ); } } public abstract class shape { public abstract double getarea (); } public interface flyable { void fly (); } record point ( int x , int y ) {} keyword meaning extends inherit from one class (or extend an interface) implements promise to provide an interface's methods super / super.method() parent constructor / parent version this / this(...) current object / another constructor abstract can't instantiate / method with no body final can't change (variable), override (method), extend (class) static belongs to the class private / protected / public class only / package + subclasses / everyone instanceof type check"}, {"id": "ref-exceptions", "title": "Exceptions", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// risky code</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileNotFoundException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// specific first</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">System</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">println</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">getMessage</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IOException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ex</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">printStackTrace</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">finally</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">// always runs</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scanner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">File</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"f.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">// auto-close</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">load</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">throws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IOException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"c1\">// declare</span>\n<span class=\"k\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IllegalArgumentException</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Bad value\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">// throw</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">MyException</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">MyException</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">super</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Unchecked (RuntimeException)</th>\n<th>Checked (must handle or declare)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NullPointerException</code></td>\n<td><code>IOException</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ArithmeticException</code></td>\n<td><code>FileNotFoundException</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException</code></td>\n<td><code>ClassNotFoundException</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>InputMismatchException</code></td>\n<td><code>CloneNotSupportedException</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NumberFormatException</code>, <code>IllegalArgumentException</code></td>\n<td><code>InterruptedException</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "try { // risky code } catch ( filenotfoundexception ex ) { // specific first system . out . println ( ex . getmessage ()); } catch ( ioexception ex ) { ex . printstacktrace (); } finally { // always runs } try ( scanner in = new scanner ( new file ( \"f.txt\" ))) { } // auto-close public void load () throws ioexception { } // declare throw new illegalargumentexception ( \"bad value\" ); // throw class myexception extends exception { myexception ( string msg ) { super ( msg ); } } unchecked (runtimeexception) checked (must handle or declare) nullpointerexception ioexception arithmeticexception filenotfoundexception arrayindexoutofboundsexception classnotfoundexception inputmismatchexception clonenotsupportedexception numberformatexception , illegalargumentexception interruptedexception"}, {"id": "ref-io", "title": "File I/O classes", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Class</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>File</code></td>\n<td>check, rename, delete files; make folders</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>PrintWriter</code></td>\n<td>write text (<code>println</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Scanner</code></td>\n<td>read text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FileInputStream</code> / <code>FileOutputStream</code></td>\n<td>read / write bytes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BufferedInputStream</code> / <code>BufferedOutputStream</code></td>\n<td>faster byte I/O</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>DataInputStream</code> / <code>DataOutputStream</code></td>\n<td>read / write primitives and UTF strings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ObjectInputStream</code> / <code>ObjectOutputStream</code></td>\n<td>read / write whole objects (<code>Serializable</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RandomAccessFile</code></td>\n<td>jump anywhere (<code>seek</code>), modes <code>\"r\"</code> / <code>\"rw\"</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>read()</code> returns <code>-1</code> at end of file.</li>\n<li>Read data back in the same order you wrote it.</li>\n</ul>", "text": "class use file check, rename, delete files; make folders printwriter write text ( println ) scanner read text fileinputstream / fileoutputstream read / write bytes bufferedinputstream / bufferedoutputstream faster byte i/o datainputstream / dataoutputstream read / write primitives and utf strings objectinputstream / objectoutputstream read / write whole objects ( serializable ) randomaccessfile jump anywhere ( seek ), modes \"r\" / \"rw\" read() returns -1 at end of file. read data back in the same order you wrote it."}, {"id": "ref-collections", "title": "Collections", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Map</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Queue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinkedList</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Stack</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Stack</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Integer</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PriorityQueue</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Key methods</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>All collections</td>\n<td><code>add</code>, <code>remove</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>isEmpty</code>, <code>contains</code>, <code>clear</code>, <code>iterator</code>, <code>forEach</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>List</td>\n<td><code>get(i)</code>, <code>set(i, x)</code>, <code>add(i, x)</code>, <code>remove(i)</code>, <code>indexOf(x)</code>, <code>sort(cmp)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stack</td>\n<td><code>push</code>, <code>pop</code>, <code>peek</code>, <code>empty</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Queue</td>\n<td><code>offer</code>, <code>poll</code>, <code>peek</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Map</td>\n<td><code>put</code>, <code>get</code>, <code>getOrDefault</code>, <code>remove</code>, <code>containsKey</code>, <code>keySet</code>, <code>values</code>, <code>entrySet</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Iterator</td>\n<td><code>hasNext</code>, <code>next</code>, <code>remove</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Collections</td>\n<td><code>sort</code>, <code>shuffle</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>reverse</code>, <code>binarySearch</code>, <code>unmodifiableList</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Hash = fast · Linked = insertion order · Tree = sorted</p>", "text": "list < string > list = new arraylist <> (); set < string > set = new hashset <> (); map < string , integer > map = new hashmap <> (); queue < string > q = new linkedlist <> (); stack < integer > stack = new stack <> (); priorityqueue < integer > pq = new priorityqueue <> (); type key methods all collections add , remove , size , isempty , contains , clear , iterator , foreach list get(i) , set(i, x) , add(i, x) , remove(i) , indexof(x) , sort(cmp) stack push , pop , peek , empty queue offer , poll , peek map put , get , getordefault , remove , containskey , keyset , values , entryset iterator hasnext , next , remove collections sort , shuffle , max , min , reverse , binarysearch , unmodifiablelist hash = fast · linked = insertion order · tree = sorted"}, {"id": "ref-javafx", "title": "JavaFX", "html": "<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Class</th>\n<th>Role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Application</code></td>\n<td>extend it; override <code>start(Stage)</code>; <code>launch(args)</code> in main</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Stage</code></td>\n<td>the window: <code>setTitle</code>, <code>setScene</code>, <code>show</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Scene</code></td>\n<td><code>new Scene(root, w, h)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Pane</code>, <code>StackPane</code>, <code>FlowPane</code>, <code>GridPane</code>, <code>BorderPane</code>, <code>HBox</code>, <code>VBox</code></td>\n<td>layouts; <code>getChildren().add(node)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Circle</code>, <code>Rectangle</code>, <code>Line</code>, <code>Ellipse</code>, <code>Polygon</code>, <code>Text</code></td>\n<td>shapes and text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Color</code>, <code>Font</code></td>\n<td><code>Color.BLUE</code>, <code>Font.font(\"Arial\", FontWeight.BOLD, 20)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Image</code>, <code>ImageView</code></td>\n<td>load / show an image</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Label</code>, <code>Button</code>, <code>CheckBox</code>, <code>RadioButton</code> + <code>ToggleGroup</code></td>\n<td>basic controls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>TextField</code>, <code>PasswordField</code>, <code>TextArea</code></td>\n<td>text input: <code>getText</code>, <code>setText</code>, <code>clear</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ComboBox</code>, <code>ListView</code></td>\n<td><code>getItems().addAll(...)</code>, <code>getValue()</code>, <code>getSelectionModel()</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Slider</code>, <code>ScrollBar</code></td>\n<td><code>valueProperty().addListener(...)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FadeTransition</code>, <code>PathTransition</code>, <code>Timeline</code> + <code>KeyFrame</code></td>\n<td>animation: <code>play</code>, <code>pause</code>, <code>stop</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Media</code>, <code>MediaPlayer</code>, <code>MediaView</code></td>\n<td>audio and video</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Event method</th>\n<th>For</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnAction(e -&gt; ...)</code></td>\n<td>buttons, Enter in TextField, ComboBox</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnMouseClicked/Pressed/Released/Moved/Dragged</code></td>\n<td>mouse (<code>e.getX()</code>, <code>e.getY()</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>setOnKeyPressed/Released/Typed</code></td>\n<td>keys (<code>e.getCode()</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>prop.bind(other)</code> / <code>bindBidirectional(other)</code></td>\n<td>keep properties in sync</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>", "text": "class role application extend it; override start(stage) ; launch(args) in main stage the window: settitle , setscene , show scene new scene(root, w, h) pane , stackpane , flowpane , gridpane , borderpane , hbox , vbox layouts; getchildren().add(node) circle , rectangle , line , ellipse , polygon , text shapes and text color , font color.blue , font.font(\"arial\", fontweight.bold, 20) image , imageview load / show an image label , button , checkbox , radiobutton + togglegroup basic controls textfield , passwordfield , textarea text input: gettext , settext , clear combobox , listview getitems().addall(...) , getvalue() , getselectionmodel() slider , scrollbar valueproperty().addlistener(...) fadetransition , pathtransition , timeline + keyframe animation: play , pause , stop media , mediaplayer , mediaview audio and video event method for setonaction(e -> ...) buttons, enter in textfield, combobox setonmouseclicked/pressed/released/moved/dragged mouse ( e.getx() , e.gety() ) setonkeypressed/released/typed keys ( e.getcode() ) prop.bind(other) / bindbidirectional(other) keep properties in sync"}, {"id": "ref-threads-tests", "title": "Threads and JUnit", "html": "<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thread</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doWork</span><span class=\"p\">());</span>\n<span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">// new thread (not run()!)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">join</span><span class=\"p\">();</span><span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"c1\">// wait for it</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">synchronized</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">increment</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<div class=\"hl\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">org.junit.jupiter.api.Test</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"nd\">@Test</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">addsNumbers</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">assertEquals</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Calculator</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">add</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">assertTrue</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">assertThrows</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IllegalArgumentException</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"na\">class</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">setAge</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>", "text": "thread t = new thread (() -> dowork ()); t . start (); // new thread (not run()!) t . join (); // wait for it public synchronized void increment () { count ++ ; } import static org.junit.jupiter.api.assertions.* ; import org.junit.jupiter.api.test ; @test void addsnumbers () { assertequals ( 7 , calculator . add ( 3 , 4 )); asserttrue ( x > 0 ); assertthrows ( illegalargumentexception . class , () -> setage ( - 1 )); }"}], "vocab": [{"title": "Foundations", "terms": [["Hardware", "The physical parts of a computer you can touch: CPU, memory, storage, monitor."], ["Software", "Programs and instructions that tell the hardware what to do."], ["CPU", "Central processing unit. Fetches instructions from memory and executes them."], ["Memory (RAM)", "Holds data and instructions while a program runs. Volatile: cleared when power is off."], ["Bit", "One binary digit, 0 or 1."], ["Byte", "8 bits."], ["Source code", "The human-written program, in a .java file."], ["Compiler", "Translates source code into a lower-level form (for Java, bytecode)."], ["Bytecode", "Compact, platform-independent instructions produced by javac and run by the JVM."], ["JVM", "Java Virtual Machine. Runs bytecode, which is what makes Java platform independent."], ["JRE", "Java Runtime Environment. What you need to run Java programs."], ["JDK", "Java Development Kit. Tools to build and run Java programs, including javac."], ["API", "Application Program Interface. The library of prewritten classes and methods."], ["Platform independent", "The same compiled program runs on any system that has a JVM."], ["IDE", "Integrated development environment (like IntelliJ IDEA) for writing, running and debugging code."], ["Syntax error", "Code that breaks Java's grammar. Caught by the compiler."], ["Runtime error", "An error that happens while the program runs and can crash it."], ["Logic error", "The program runs but gives the wrong result."], ["Variable", "A named memory location that stores a value of one type."], ["Identifier", "The name of a variable, method, class or constant."], ["Constant", "A value that can't change, declared with final."], ["Literal", "A fixed value written directly in code, like 100 or \"hi\"."], ["Primitive type", "A basic built-in type that holds its value directly: int, double, char, boolean and so on."], ["Casting", "Converting a value from one type to another, like (int) 9.7."], ["Widening", "Converting a smaller type to a larger one (int → double). Automatic."], ["Narrowing", "Converting a larger type to a smaller one (double → int). Needs an explicit cast."], ["Overflow", "A value too large for its type, which wraps around to a wrong value."], ["Integer division", "Dividing two ints, which drops the decimal part (5 / 2 is 2)."], ["IPO", "Input, Process, Output: a way to plan what a program does."], ["Pseudocode", "A plain-English plan for code."], ["Incremental coding", "Writing and testing a program one small piece at a time."]]}, {"title": "Decisions and loops", "terms": [["Boolean expression", "An expression that evaluates to true or false."], ["Selection statement", "A statement that chooses a path: if, if-else, switch."], ["Short-circuit evaluation", "&& and || stop as soon as the result is known."], ["Dangling else", "An else that attaches to the nearest if, which may not be the one intended."], ["Fall-through", "In a switch without break, execution continues into the next case."], ["Conditional operator", "The ternary operator cond ? a : b, a one-line if-else that produces a value."], ["Operator precedence", "The order in which operators are evaluated."], ["Operator associativity", "Which direction operators of equal precedence group (most left to right; assignment right to left)."], ["Iteration", "One pass through a loop."], ["Loop body", "The code a loop repeats."], ["Pretest loop", "Checks its condition before each pass (while, for)."], ["Posttest loop", "Checks its condition after each pass, so it runs at least once (do-while)."], ["Infinite loop", "A loop whose condition never becomes false."], ["Sentinel value", "A special input value that signals the loop to stop."], ["Nested loop", "A loop inside another loop."], ["Off-by-one error", "A loop or index that goes one step too far or not far enough."], ["break", "Leaves the loop immediately."], ["continue", "Skips the rest of the current pass and starts the next one."]]}, {"title": "Strings, characters and Math", "terms": [["char", "A type that stores one character, written in single quotes."], ["Unicode", "The character encoding Java uses, covering many languages and symbols."], ["ASCII", "An older encoding with values 0–127 ('A' is 65)."], ["Escape sequence", "A backslash code for a special character, like \\n or \\t."], ["Whitespace character", "A space, tab or newline."], ["Instance method", "A method called on an object, like word.length()."], ["Static method", "A method called on the class, like Math.sqrt(25)."], ["Format specifier", "A placeholder in printf, like %d or %.2f."], ["Immutable", "Can't be changed after it's created. Strings are immutable."], ["String pool", "A shared memory area where Java keeps string literals."], ["StringBuilder", "A mutable string class, faster for building up text."]]}, {"title": "Methods", "terms": [["Method", "A named, reusable block of code that performs a task."], ["Parameter (formal)", "A variable listed in a method's header."], ["Argument (actual parameter)", "A value passed into a method when it's called."], ["Return value", "The value a method sends back to its caller."], ["Void method", "A method that doesn't return a value."], ["Method signature", "A method's name plus its parameter list (not the return type)."], ["Method overloading", "Several methods with the same name but different parameter lists."], ["Ambiguous invocation", "A call that matches two overloads equally well. A compile error."], ["Pass-by-value", "Java passes copies of values into methods; for objects, a copy of the reference."], ["Scope", "The part of the program where a variable exists."], ["Local variable", "A variable declared inside a method or block."], ["Method abstraction", "Using a method without knowing how it works inside."], ["Information hiding", "Keeping implementation details hidden behind a method or class interface."], ["Stepwise refinement", "Breaking a big problem into smaller methods."], ["Stub", "A temporary empty method used while building a program."], ["Recursion", "A method that calls itself on a smaller version of the problem."], ["Base case", "The condition that stops recursion."]]}, {"title": "Arrays", "terms": [["Array", "A fixed-size collection of elements of the same type."], ["Index", "The position of an element. Starts at 0."], ["Indexed variable", "An array element accessed by its index, like nums[2]."], ["Array initializer", "Shortcut syntax that creates and fills an array: {1, 2, 3}."], ["Anonymous array", "An array created without a variable to hold it."], ["Varargs", "A parameter like int... nums that accepts any number of arguments."], ["Linear search", "Checking elements one at a time. O(n)."], ["Binary search", "Repeatedly halving a sorted array to find a value. O(log n)."], ["Selection sort", "Repeatedly selecting the smallest remaining value and swapping it into place. O(n²)."], ["Precondition", "What must be true before a method runs."], ["Postcondition", "What is true after a method finishes."], ["Two-dimensional array", "An array of arrays, used as a table of rows and columns."], ["Ragged array", "A 2D array whose rows have different lengths."], ["Garbage collection", "The JVM automatically freeing memory that nothing refers to."]]}, {"title": "Objects and classes", "terms": [["Class", "A blueprint or template for objects."], ["Object", "An instance of a class, with state, behavior and identity."], ["Constructor", "A special method that initializes a new object. Same name as the class, no return type."], ["Instance variable", "A field that belongs to each object separately."], ["Static variable", "A field shared by all objects of the class."], ["Reference variable", "A variable that holds a reference (address) to an object."], ["null", "The value of a reference that points to no object."], ["UML", "Unified Modeling Language. Diagrams of classes and their relationships."], ["this", "Refers to the current object."], ["Encapsulation", "Protecting data by making fields private and giving controlled access through methods."], ["Getter (accessor)", "A method that returns a field's value."], ["Setter (mutator)", "A method that changes a field's value."], ["Immutable class", "A class whose objects can't change after creation."], ["Class abstraction", "Separating what a class does from how it does it."], ["Class contract", "The public methods and the promises about what they do."], ["Abstract data type (ADT)", "A type defined by its behavior, not its implementation."], ["Aggregation", "A weak has-a relationship; the parts can exist on their own."], ["Composition", "A strong has-a relationship; the part can't exist without the whole."], ["Multiplicity", "How many objects take part in a relationship."], ["Cohesion", "How focused a class is on one purpose."], ["Wrapper class", "An object version of a primitive, like Integer for int."], ["Boxing / unboxing", "Automatic conversion between a primitive and its wrapper."], ["BigInteger / BigDecimal", "Classes for very large integers and exact decimals."], ["Inheritance", "A subclass reusing and extending a superclass."], ["Superclass", "The parent class being inherited from."], ["Subclass", "The child class that inherits."], ["Is-a relationship", "The test for using inheritance: a Dog is an Animal."], ["super", "Refers to the superclass: its constructor or its version of a method."], ["Constructor chaining", "Constructors calling each other up the inheritance chain."], ["Method overriding", "A subclass providing its own version of an inherited method."], ["@Override", "An annotation asking the compiler to check that a method really overrides one."], ["Object class", "The root class every Java class inherits from."], ["Polymorphism", "A superclass variable can refer to any subclass object, and the right overridden method runs."], ["Dynamic binding", "Choosing which overridden method to run at runtime, based on the actual object."], ["Abstract class", "A class that can't be instantiated; may contain abstract methods."], ["Abstract method", "A method with no body that subclasses must implement."], ["Interface", "A set of behaviors a class promises to provide."], ["Subinterface", "An interface that extends another interface."], ["Marker interface", "An empty interface that marks a capability, like Cloneable or Serializable."], ["Comparable", "Interface that gives a class a natural ordering via compareTo."], ["Comparator", "An outside rule for comparing two objects."], ["Shallow copy", "A copy that shares inner objects with the original."], ["Deep copy", "A copy that also duplicates inner objects, fully independent."], ["Record", "A compact, immutable data class with generated methods."]]}, {"title": "Exceptions and file I/O", "terms": [["Exception", "An object representing an error or unexpected event while running."], ["Checked exception", "An exception the compiler forces you to handle or declare."], ["Unchecked exception", "A RuntimeException or Error; not checked by the compiler."], ["throw", "Creates and throws an exception."], ["throws", "Declares in a method header that it may throw an exception."], ["Exception propagation", "An uncaught exception passing up the chain of method calls."], ["Chained exception", "An exception that carries the original exception that caused it."], ["finally", "A block that always runs after try/catch."], ["try-with-resources", "A try that automatically closes the resources it opens."], ["Absolute path", "A full file path from the root."], ["Relative path", "A file path from the current folder."], ["Stream", "A flow of data into or out of a program."], ["Text I/O", "Reading and writing human-readable characters."], ["Binary I/O", "Reading and writing raw bytes."], ["Buffering", "Grouping data into chunks to reduce slow disk access."], ["Serialization", "Converting an object into bytes for storage."], ["Deserialization", "Rebuilding an object from bytes."], ["Sequential access", "Reading a file in order from start to end."], ["Random access", "Jumping to any position in a file."], ["File pointer", "The current byte position in a random-access file."], ["Web crawler", "A program that follows links from page to page."]]}, {"title": "Collections", "terms": [["Collection", "A group of objects treated as a single unit."], ["Data structure", "A way of organizing data."], ["Java Collections Framework", "The interfaces and classes for storing and manipulating groups of objects."], ["Generics", "Type parameters like <String> that tell the compiler what a collection holds."], ["Iterator", "An object for stepping through a collection one element at a time."], ["List", "An ordered collection that allows duplicates and index access."], ["Linked list", "Nodes connected by references."], ["Stack", "Last-in, first-out (LIFO)."], ["Queue", "First-in, first-out (FIFO)."], ["Priority queue", "Removes the highest-priority (smallest) element first."], ["Set", "A collection of unique elements."], ["HashSet / LinkedHashSet / TreeSet", "Sets that are unordered / insertion-ordered / sorted."], ["Map", "Key → value pairs with unique keys."], ["HashMap / LinkedHashMap / TreeMap", "Maps that are unordered / ordered / sorted by key."], ["Unmodifiable collection", "A read-only view of a collection."], ["Vector", "An older, synchronized version of ArrayList."]]}, {"title": "JavaFX", "terms": [["Stage", "The window."], ["Scene", "The container inside a stage that holds all the content."], ["Node", "Any visual element: panes, controls, shapes, text, images."], ["Root node", "The top node in a scene, usually a pane."], ["Pane", "A container that lays out its child nodes."], ["Property binding", "Linking properties so one updates automatically when another changes."], ["Observable object", "An object that notifies listeners when its value changes."], ["Listener", "Code that runs when an observable value changes."], ["Event-driven programming", "Code that waits for and responds to user actions."], ["Event", "An action such as a click or key press."], ["Event source", "The object that fires an event."], ["Event handler", "Code that responds to an event."], ["Inner class", "A class defined inside another class."], ["Anonymous inner class", "An unnamed class defined and created in one expression."], ["Lambda expression", "A short way to implement a functional interface."], ["Functional interface (SAM)", "An interface with exactly one abstract method."], ["ToggleGroup", "Groups radio buttons so only one can be selected."], ["ObservableList", "A list that updates the UI when its data changes."]]}, {"title": "Concurrency and testing", "terms": [["Thread", "A separate path of execution inside a program."], ["Runnable", "An interface whose run() method holds a thread's task."], ["Race condition", "Threads changing shared data at the same time, causing unpredictable results."], ["synchronized", "Lets only one thread at a time run that code on the same object."], ["Deadlock", "Threads each waiting forever for a lock another holds."], ["Unit test", "An automatic check of one small part of a program."], ["Assertion", "A statement in a test that must be true for the test to pass."], ["Boundary case", "A test at the edge of valid input, like 0 or the maximum."]]}], "res": [{"title": "Main references", "items": [{"title": "Dev.java Learn Java", "url": "https://dev.java/learn/", "note": "Your main reference. Official, current lessons on basics, classes, inheritance, collections, exceptions and I/O."}, {"title": "Java Programming MOOC (University of Helsinki)", "url": "https://java-programming.mooc.fi/", "note": "Clear, classroom-style explanations with lots of exercises. Use it when you want a slower walkthrough."}, {"title": "Oracle Java Tutorials", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/", "note": "Still good for established topics, though some pages cover older Java versions."}, {"title": "Java 21 API documentation", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/", "note": "Every class and method in your Java version. Search a class name to see all its methods."}]}, {"title": "Practice", "items": [{"title": "Exercism Java track", "url": "https://exercism.org/tracks/java", "note": "Your main practice site. Free exercises grouped by concept, with optional mentoring."}, {"title": "JetBrains Academy", "url": "https://www.jetbrains.com/academy/", "note": "Project-based learning that plugs into IntelliJ."}]}, {"title": "Topic deep dives", "items": [{"title": "Object-Oriented Programming Concepts (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/java/concepts/", "note": "Objects, classes, inheritance, interfaces, packages."}, {"title": "Interfaces and Inheritance (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/java/IandI/", "note": "Overriding, polymorphism, abstract classes, interfaces."}, {"title": "Collections (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/collections/", "note": "Lists, sets, maps, queues and algorithms."}, {"title": "Object Ordering (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/collections/interfaces/order.html", "note": "Comparable and Comparator in depth."}, {"title": "Exceptions (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/essential/exceptions/", "note": "Catching, throwing, checked vs unchecked."}, {"title": "Concurrency (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/essential/concurrency/", "note": "Threads, synchronization, thread interference, deadlock."}, {"title": "Guarded Blocks: producer–consumer (Oracle)", "url": "https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/essential/concurrency/guardmeth.html", "note": "Threads sharing data and coordinating with wait() and notify()."}, {"title": "JUnit", "url": "https://junit.org/", "note": "Official site and user guide for writing unit tests."}, {"title": "OpenJFX", "url": "https://openjfx.io/", "note": "JavaFX downloads and getting-started docs, including IntelliJ setup."}]}], "files": [["Chapter study guides [1]–[21]", "Intro, basics, selections, math/chars/strings, loops, methods, arrays, 2D arrays, objects and classes, OOP thinking, superclasses, exceptions, abstract classes, JavaFX (3 guides), I/O, lists/stacks/queues, sets and maps. In your java study folder."], ["learning_java.docx", "Your learning plan: resources, explanations and practice projects. Its schedule was left out here on purpose."], ["JavaCheatSheet.pdf and java_cheat_sheet.pdf", "Two one-page cheat sheets, folded into the Quick reference tab."]]};
